    #      the local headers: for a changed entry whose bit 3 both sides keep,
    #      that is P1's "when the input sets bit 3", and a recompressed one's
    #      descriptor carries its new compressed size. The lines' relations are
    #      the spec's: anchor two images, anchors and media entries more, one
    #      image of each anchor kind more; removeimage images_after the images
    #      less kept_removed, media_dropped the entries gone, 0 with nothing kept
    #      removed. The tool's counts equal the comparison's.
    #  VD. NEW, the survey (imgsurvey.py, <scripts>, copied into <work> and
    #      printed) replaces UD's, in its form: <corpus> its parameter, every
    #      regular file of <corpus>/corpus listed, one wb line of thirteen
    #      fields per workbook, one drawings line (decision 8: the drawing parts
    #      and the largest drawing's anchor count, printed); the log checks its
    #      forms, prints the distributions and checks every line's figures
    #      against it, and the comparison's parts against it.
    #  VE. Changes PE, QE and SE (every row ok) stand. The entries rules: anchor
    #      is M2 part 4d P3's image rule with two media entries; removeimage is
    #      the planning rulings during P2: with nothing kept removed, W, W's rels
    #      part, the content types and a drawing that stays identical or
    #      recompressed, its rels part changed with the same relationships
    #      allowed (ruling 1); at most one added row, W's rels part or the
    #      drawing's where the input has none, its root childless (ruling 2);
    #      an empty input drawing dropped with W, W's rels part and the content
    #      types changed or recompressed (ruling 3); with the first image
    #      removed, the spec's: the drawing and its rels part changed, the media
    #      entries the count rule drops dropped, the content types changed where
    #      an Override went. Each allowance has a control that accepts it where
    #      it applies and one that refuses it where it does not. The removal's
    #      summary totals are checked against its entries table, every row by
    #      the rule.
    #  VF. NEW, the comment box sample once more on both targets, its outputs
    #      by sha256, its lines and its diff tables P1's run's byte for byte, the
    #      run directory named by P1's record commit through the run record it
    #      added (M3 part 5 P3's change WC form); no record pair is written for
    #      the rerun.
    #  VG. Change UG's no-row rule stands: neither sample writes a cell, so the
    #      calculation chain's entry stays identical (change UF).
    #  VH. Change PH (the open check's own TMPDIR device) stands, unchanged.
    #  VI. The plants: every flag's planted control runs, for each sample, on
    #      the first ok workbook in manifest order of its created case (anchor:
    #      W has no drawing; removeimage: no image is kept and W has no drawing)
    #      and of its kept case (anchor: W has a drawing; removeimage: the first
    #      image is removed), each on its own check line, the plant turning its
    #      own flag; kept_children on the anchor's created case has no kept
    #      child to change, and its line checks the plant reports planted=no
    #      there and the flag stays yes; the anchor's kept case is a drawing
    #      with a root child (an empty drawing gives the case other). The xml
    #      values check wants some value written by the anchor sample and some
    #      removed by the removal, which writes none (change LF's form).
    #  VJ. The run loop, the record pairs, the keep and the open check are SJ's
    #      and WJ's with this phase's names; reccheck.py takes the dropped
    #      families as an input beside the changed and added ones; the anchor
    #      record's families are derived from the --parts lines, the removal
    #      record's from its entries table, which the rule checked row by row
    #      (the rulings allow a row recompressed or changed); six record files
    #      installed, four when the keep is skipped.
    #  VK. UK stands: this script runs no `rm -rf`; the sourced
    #      scripts/counting.sh, a committed script, runs one on the directory its
    #      counting controls make (allowed: a directory the script created in
    #      that run); the working directory and the keeps stand, kept, and
    #      Python writes no bytecode.
    #
    #
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 6 P3 from M3 part 6 P2's run script (at the phase
    # commit d3c4a9c, printed in records/logs/m3p6-p2/run.log; its change lists
    # up to VK are above), generated by <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p6-p3/gen/
    # run.py, every replacement asserted to occur as often as it says, the top
    # summary and the body from the survey to the corpus record pairs'
    # installation replaced whole (gen/run_block.sh, by its anchor lines, P2's
    # record check carried into it unchanged), and the body grepped afterwards
    # for P2's names, subjects, stems and the tokens imgcmp, imgsurvey,
    # m3p6-p2-, P1_REC and PREV_CB. What differs, and why:
    #  XA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects, the script directory
    #      (<scripts>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p6-p3/scripts, on the disk)
    #      and the keep (m3p6-p3/keep-host) are this phase's; the base is P2's
    #      record commit ("M3 part 6 P2 record:"); the phase commit is P3's tool
    #      commit by its subject ("M3 part 6 P3: emend-copy --copy-sample"); one
    #      sample, copy, with its run directory <runs>/<date>-<sha>-copy and its
    #      record stem m3p6-p3-<date>-<sha> (the spec's name), and three rerun
    #      directories <runs>/<date>-<sha>-anchor, -removeimage and -commentbox
    #      (RERUNS); SUPERSEDED_RUN names the four by their common stem; the
    #      spec pinned through SPEC_SHA at P3's doc commit, planning's rulings
    #      during P3 standing uncommitted in the working tree's copy, printed.
    #  XB. Change VB's form: the committed open-check record the keep is
    #      compared with is P2's, the last committed, named by its record
    #      commit, resolved by its subject ("M3 part 6 P2 record:"; no hash is
    #      typed here); it is the base itself, the parent of P3's doc commit; the
    #      control names the doc commit instead. P2_REC names the same commit, the
    #      one whose run directories the reruns are compared with (change XF).
    #  XC. The comparison is copycmp.py, built for this phase (<home>/.cache/
    #      emend-build/m3p6-p3/gen/copycmp_build.py) with P2's imgcmp.py
    #      readers copied by name, one mode, copy, fifteen flags: whole_bytes,
    #      data_same, kept_same, views_same, setup_same, dropped_gone (the
    #      spec's copy check, and the copy built from S byte for byte),
    #      rels_set (ruling 1), comments_same and notes_placed (the spec's
    #      carried checks), workbook_sheet, types_set, chain_rule, rest_same,
    #      xml_values and flagged (P2's). The lines' relations are the spec's:
    #      one sheet more, the copy's counts its source's, no chain after a
    #      formula. The tool's counts equal the comparison's.
    #  XD. NEW, the survey (copysurvey.py, <scripts>, copied into <work> and
    #      printed) replaces VD's, in its form: <corpus> its parameter, every
    #      regular file of <corpus>/corpus listed, one wb line of twenty fields
    #      per workbook; the log checks its forms, prints the distributions and
    #      checks every line's figures against it, and the comparison's parts
    #      against it. No drawings line (no decision rests on one here).
    #  XE. Changes PE, QE, SE and VE (every row ok) stand. The entries rule is
    #      the rulings during P3's: the copy's entry added; its rels part added
    #      exactly when S has a hyperlink or a comments relationship (ruling 1);
    #      the comments and VML parts added when carried; the workbook part, its
    #      rels part and the content types changed, flagged descriptor at most;
    #      the chain's entry dropped exactly when S holds a formula and the
    #      workbook a chain; every other row identical and unflagged; nothing
    #      recompressed. Each allowance has a control that accepts it where it
    #      applies and one that refuses it where it does not. The summary's
    #      totals are checked against what the rows imply and against the
    #      entries table.
    #  XF. NEW, the three earlier samples once more on both targets, their
    #      outputs by sha256, their lines and their diff tables P2's runs' byte
    #      for byte (change VF's form for three samples), the run directories
    #      read from the "the run directories:" line of P2's run log at P2's
    #      record commit and checked against the run directory P2's committed
    #      anchor record names; no record pair is written for the reruns.
    #  XG. Change UG's no-row rule gives way: the copy makes the write a formula
    #      change when S holds a formula (specs/0013's rule, "The copy"), so
    #      each chain workbook's calcChain row is dropped exactly there, and is
    #      identical and unflagged elsewhere; some row is dropped.
    #  XH. Change PH (the open check's own TMPDIR device) stands, unchanged.
    #  XI. The plants: every flag's planted control runs on the first ok
    #      workbook in manifest order of the plain case (S's comments not
    #      carried) and of the carried case, each on its own check line, the
    #      plant turning its own flag; every flag has a plant on both cases.
    #      The xml values check wants some value written (the workbook's new
    #      sheet; change LF's form).
    #  XJ. The run loop, the record pair, the keep and the open check are VJ's
    #      with this phase's names; the record's families are derived from its
    #      entries table, which the rule checked row by row; four record files
    #      installed, two when the keep is skipped.
    #  XK. Ruling 8 of the planning rulings during P2 (build pruning) and
    #      ruling 10 of the planning rulings during P3 (one target root per
    #      phase, one subdirectory per source tree): the phase's target root is
    #      <target>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p6-p3/target, and every build
    #      of <repo> by this script, dry or logged, goes into <target>/main
    #      (CARGO_TARGET_DIR), the subdirectory ruling 10 gives the main tree;
    #      this script builds from no other tree. P2's <build> placeholder (a
    #      run directory holding its own target) is gone with the input
    #      RUN_BUILD_ROOT, so no run moves the builds, and nothing here cleans
    #      them; the i686 keep is <work>/keep-i686, kept, not under the target.
    #      VK stands: this script runs no `rm -rf`.
    #
    # Usage: m6p1-p3-run.sh <phase commit> [<size log>] > <file outside the tree>;
    # the caller moves the output to records/logs/m6p1-p3/run.log (changes NXG
    # and NXH).
    set -uo pipefail
    SELF_DIR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
    SELF=$SELF_DIR/$(basename "$0")
    # specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7: this script's own standard error, kept and counted at the end.
    mkdir -p "$SELF_DIR/out" || exit 2
    ERR=$SELF_DIR/out/run.stderr
    exec 2>"$ERR"
    cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 2
    MAIN=$(pwd)
    
    C=${1:?phase commit required}
    # Every environment input, as it was set, before any is unset.
    INPUT_NAMES="RUN_SUFFIX SUPERSEDED_RUN SUPERSEDED_KEEP RERUN_NOTE RERUN_FILES RECORDS_DEST RUN_KEEP RUN_OUT_ROOT RUN_SKIP_KEEP SIZE_BUILD_ROOT PLANNING_SPEC EMEND_CORPUS_DIR EMEND_KEEP_DIR HOME"
    declare -A INPUT_SEEN
    for v in $INPUT_NAMES; do
      if [ -n "${!v+x}" ]; then INPUT_SEEN[$v]=${!v}; else INPUT_SEEN[$v]=unset; fi
    done
    CORPUS=${EMEND_CORPUS_DIR:-$HOME/emend-testing}
    export RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0 CARGO_TERM_COLOR=never CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4
    # Python writes no bytecode, so nothing arises to be removed.
    export PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
    # Change NTK (M5 part 1 P3's NTC, carried): every cargo command of this log
    # runs offline; the two settings are printed below.
    export CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true
    unset EMEND_KEEP_DIR EMEND_CORPUS_DIR RUSTDOCFLAGS RUSTFLAGS
    IMAGE=localhost/emend-lo:25.2.3-2-deb13u6
    LO_TIMEOUT_S=600
    SPEC=specs/0038-chartsheets.md
    # Change NXG: the committed blob the doc commit 8910350 holds (planning's
    # P3 brief, by hash).
    SPEC_WANT=f15be1a082884c256c102345554d1f12506e92d49132438afd288bf065bad65b
    # Change NWS: the one sample, with its tool argument.
    SAMPLES="chartsheet"
    declare -A EDITS=([chartsheet]=--chartsheet-sample)
    PLANNING_SPEC=${PLANNING_SPEC:-}
    PHASE_DIR=$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m6p1-p3
    # Change NXJ: P2's phase directory, where P2's run kept its working
    # directory and its openpyxl fixture; read only.
    P2_PHASE=$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m6p1-p2
    # Change NSK: every build of <repo>, dry or logged, goes into the main tree's
    # subdirectory of the phase's one target root, <target>/main; no input moves
    # it and nothing here cleans it. The logged run leaves RUN_KEEP unset; a dry
    # run points it elsewhere so it leaves no keep where the logged run refuses
    # one.
    TARGET_ROOT=$PHASE_DIR/target
    BUILD_ROOT=$TARGET_ROOT/main
    # Change NXH (M5 part 6 P3's NWA, carried): the size log and its build
    # directory, whose release binaries every run below uses.
    SIZE_LOG=${2:-$PHASE_DIR/logs/size.log}
    SIZE_BUILD=${SIZE_BUILD_ROOT:-$TARGET_ROOT/main}
    KEEP=${RUN_KEEP:-$PHASE_DIR/keep-host}
    RUN_OUT_ROOT=${RUN_OUT_ROOT:-$CORPUS/runs}
    RUN_SKIP_KEEP=${RUN_SKIP_KEEP:-no}
    case $RUN_SKIP_KEEP in yes | no) ;; *) echo "RUN_SKIP_KEEP is yes or no" >&2; exit 2 ;; esac
    INSTALLED=()
    I686=i686-unknown-linux-musl
    RECORDS_DEST=${RECORDS_DEST:-records}
    # A keep in place is another attempt's, moved below once the header can list
    # it; without SUPERSEDED_KEEP naming the attempt it is refused.
    SUPERSEDED_KEEP=${SUPERSEDED_KEEP:-}
    case $SUPERSEDED_KEEP in '' | attempt-[1-9]) ;; *) echo "SUPERSEDED_KEEP is attempt-<n> or nothing" >&2; exit 2 ;; esac
    if [ "$RUN_SKIP_KEEP" = no ] && [ -e "$KEEP" ] && [ -z "$SUPERSEDED_KEEP" ]; then echo "$KEEP is already there; name its attempt in SUPERSEDED_KEEP" >&2; exit 2; fi
    mkdir -p "$BUILD_ROOT" || exit 2
    export CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$BUILD_ROOT
    # Change NWS: a dry run (RECORDS_DEST other than records) stages its
    # records in RECORDS_DEST/staged, so it leaves nothing in
    # <scripts>/out/records for the logged run to refuse.
    if [ "$RECORDS_DEST" = records ]; then RECORDS=$SELF_DIR/out/records; else RECORDS=$RECORDS_DEST/staged; fi
    # Change NTI: TMPDIR is <scratch>/tmp, the phase's directory's, made and
    # exported before any mktemp (close-out ruling 1); the working directory
    # is the one mktemp -d makes under it, on the disk, kept; nothing here is
    # removed.
    TMPDIR=$PHASE_DIR/tmp
    export TMPDIR
    mkdir -p "$TMPDIR" || exit 2
    B=$(mktemp -d) || exit 2
    # Change NSB: the counting library is the phase commit's, by git show.
    git show "$C:scripts/counting.sh" >"$B/counting.sh" || exit 2
    . "$B/counting.sh"
    fail=0
    check() { echo "  $1: $2"; [ "$2" = yes ] || fail=1; }
    yn() { if "$@"; then echo yes; else echo no; fi; }
    # For a condition that must NOT hold: a leading bang inside yn runs a
    # command named by the bang (specs/0001), so a negation has its own helper.
    ynnot() { if "$@"; then echo no; else echo yes; fi; }
    TAB=$(printf '\t')
    sha_of() { sha256sum <"$1" | cut -d' ' -f1; }
    
    head_is() { [ "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = "$1" ]; }
    full_sha() { printf '%s' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'; }
    # The given commit is the phase commit when it is a full sha and HEAD.
    given_ok() { full_sha "$1" && head_is "$1"; }
    if given_ok "$C"; then :; else echo "the phase commit must be a full 40-hex sha that is HEAD, not $C" >&2; exit 2; fi
    NULL_SHA=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
    case "${C: -1}" in 0) LAST=1 ;; *) LAST=0 ;; esac
    FAKE_SHA=${C:0:39}$LAST
    SHORT=$(git rev-parse --short=7 "$C")
    DATE=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%d)
    # What the status pattern admits (changes NSB, NUB, NUI and NXG): this
    # phase's log directory, this phase's two record pairs (named by the run's
    # date and the phase commit's short sha, untracked), the API record the
    # test log writes and the size record the size log writes (any date, the
    # phase commit's short sha, untracked), and specs/0038 and ROADMAP.md
    # modified should planning hold a ruling during P3 uncommitted; nothing
    # else.
    OURS="^((\\?\\?| ?[MARCD]) records/logs/m6p1-p3/|\\?\\? records/m6p1-(p3-chartsheet|open)-$DATE-$SHORT[.](md|txt)\$|\\?\\? records/(api-review|size)-m6p1-[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-$SHORT[.]md\$| M specs/0038-chartsheets[.]md\$| M ROADMAP[.]md\$)"
    entry_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    entry_ours=$(run_matches -E "$OURS" git status --porcelain)
    entry_clean() { [ "$entry_all" != error ] && [ "$entry_ours" != error ] && [ "$entry_all" = "$entry_ours" ]; }
    if entry_clean; then :; else
      echo "the working tree holds changes outside this phase's logs, its records, the API and size records and planning's spec and roadmap" >&2
      exit 2
    fi
    # Change NXG: the one sample's record stem, the phase's, with the
    # sample's word (specs/0038 "P3": m6p1-p3-<sample>-<utc-date>-<shortsha>).
    declare -A STEMS=([chartsheet]=m6p1-p3-chartsheet-$DATE-$SHORT)
    STEM_OPEN=m6p1-open-$DATE-$SHORT
    # A rerun takes a suffix, so its run directory is never the superseded one.
    RUN_SUFFIX=${RUN_SUFFIX:-}
    case $RUN_SUFFIX in '' | -[b-z]) ;; *) echo "RUN_SUFFIX is -b to -z or nothing" >&2; exit 2 ;; esac
    RUN=$DATE-$SHORT$RUN_SUFFIX
    mkdir -p "$RECORDS" "$RECORDS_DEST" || exit 2
    # A rerun names the superseded run directory, which is MOVED into
    # <scripts>/out/superseded after the header prints it, never removed; it
    # must be another run of this phase, not this one.
    SUPERSEDED_RUN=${SUPERSEDED_RUN:-}
    case $SUPERSEDED_RUN in
      '' | 20[0-9][0-9]-[01][0-9]-[0-3][0-9]-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f] | 20[0-9][0-9]-[01][0-9]-[0-3][0-9]-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]-[b-z]) ;;
      *) echo "SUPERSEDED_RUN is not a run directory's name" >&2; exit 2 ;;
    esac
    if [ -n "$SUPERSEDED_RUN" ] && [ "$SUPERSEDED_RUN" = "$RUN" ]; then echo "SUPERSEDED_RUN names this run's own directory" >&2; exit 2; fi
    for f in "$RECORDS/$STEM_OPEN.md" "$RECORDS/$STEM_OPEN.txt" "$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM_OPEN.md" "$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM_OPEN.txt" \
             "$RECORDS/${STEMS[chartsheet]}.md" "$RECORDS/${STEMS[chartsheet]}.txt" "$RECORDS_DEST/${STEMS[chartsheet]}.md" "$RECORDS_DEST/${STEMS[chartsheet]}.txt"; do
      if [ -e "$f" ]; then echo "$f is already there; move it aside first" >&2; exit 2; fi
    done
    # A run directory that exists before the run is another attempt's; refused
    # (the runner itself refuses one holding an earlier run's conversion
    # directories, specs/0030 decision 1 A).
    # Change NVX: each sample's run directory (one, change NWS).
    for s in $SAMPLES; do
      if [ -e "$RUN_OUT_ROOT/$RUN-$s" ]; then echo "$RUN_OUT_ROOT/$RUN-$s is already there; name a fresh run" >&2; exit 2; fi
    done
    
    # The corpus's path begins with <repo>'s, so <runs> and <corpus> are
    # replaced before <repo> (M4 part 1 P3's order); the phase's directories
    # before <phase>, and <home> last.
    scrub() {
      sed -e "s#$B#<work>#g" -e "s#$TMPDIR#<scratch>/tmp#g" -e "s#$SELF_DIR#<scripts>#g" -e "s#$KEEP#<keep>#g" \
        -e "s#$TARGET_ROOT#<target>#g" -e "s#$RUN_OUT_ROOT#<runs>#g" -e "s#$CORPUS#<corpus>#g" \
        -e "s#$MAIN#<repo>#g" -e "s#$PHASE_DIR#<phase>#g" -e "s#$P2_PHASE#<p2phase>#g" -e "s#$HOME#<home>#g"
    }
    exec 3>&1
    exec > >(scrub >&3)
    SCRUB_PID=$!
    
    echo "command: git rev-parse HEAD"
    echo "invocation: bash <scripts>/$(basename "$0") $*"
    echo "about: M6 part 1 P3 phase commit $C; HEAD at run: $(git rev-parse HEAD)"
    # The environment inputs, each on its labelled line.
    for v in $INPUT_NAMES; do echo "input: $v=${INPUT_SEEN[$v]}"; done
    echo "input (as exported by this script, change NTK): PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=$PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=$CARGO_NET_OFFLINE"
    echo "input: TMPDIR=$TMPDIR"
    echo "  (TMPDIR set, made and exported by this script before any mktemp; <work> is made under it: close-out ruling 1; change NTI)"
    echo "input: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: $([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] && echo set || echo unset) (its value never printed)"
    echo
    echo "## the three shape greps, over this script, before its log (specs/0001)"
    D='$'
    SHAPE_CHAIN="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) .*(&&|\\|\\|)"
    SHAPE_BANG="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) !"
    SHAPE_ASSIGN="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*="
    printf '%s\n' "x=${D}(is [ 1 ] && true)" "y=${D}(isnot ! true)" "z=${D}(yn N=1 true)" >"$B/shape-fixture"
    echo "command: count_matches -E <shape> <this script>, and the same over a fixture holding one line of each shape"
    for shape in CHAIN BANG ASSIGN; do
      var=SHAPE_$shape
      n_self=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$SELF")
      n_fix=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$B/shape-fixture")
      echo "  shape $shape: in this script $n_self; in the fixture $n_fix"
      check "$shape: this script holds none" "$(yn [ "$n_self" = 0 ])"
      check "control: $shape: the same form finds the fixture's one line" "$(yn [ "$n_fix" = 1 ])"
    done
    check "control: ynnot reports no on a passing command" "$(yn [ "$(ynnot true)" = no ])"
    # Change NTJ: the fourth shape, PYB: a Python call without -I -B (the word
    # followed by whitespace and an option or a .py path, outside a comment,
    # and not by " -I -B"). The word is built from two halves, so that this
    # form's own text is no call.
    PYW=pyth
    PYW=${PYW}on3
    pyb_count() {
      awk -v w="$PYW" '{ l = $0; sub(/^[ \t]+/, "", l); if (substr(l, 1, 1) == "#") next; s = l
        while ((i = index(s, w)) > 0) { r = substr(s, i + length(w)); if (r ~ /^[ \t]+(-|[^ \t]*[.]py([ \t"]|$))/ && r !~ /^ -I -B( |$)/) { n++; break }; s = r }
      } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"
    }
    printf '%s\n' "$PYW -c x" "$PYW -I -B -c x" "# $PYW -c x" "command -v $PYW" "$PYW tool.py" >"$B/pyb-fixture"
    n_self=$(pyb_count "$SELF")
    n_fix=$(pyb_count "$B/pyb-fixture")
    echo "command: pyb_count <this script>, and the same over a fixture of five lines: a call with -c, one with -I -B -c, a comment, a command -v, a call of a .py path"
    echo "  shape PYB: in this script $n_self; in the fixture $n_fix"
    check "PYB: this script holds none (change NTJ)" "$(yn [ "$n_self" = 0 ])"
    check "control: PYB: the same form finds the fixture's two calls without -I -B and not its other three lines" "$(yn [ "$n_fix" = 2 ])"
    # Rulings Z, AD and AK a (change NWT): the defined-helper check over this
    # script's own source, and its planted controls. The program is written
    # into <work> from this script's text, so nothing is copied beside it; the
    # planted calls are built from pieces, so this text holds no call of an
    # undefined name.
    cat >"$B/defined_check.py" <<'PY'
    """The defined-helper check (specs/0037: ruling Q, carried into each script's
    own shape block by ruling Z, widened by rulings AD and AK a): every helper
    a yn, ynnot, is or isnot call names is defined in the script, and each of
    the four the script calls is itself defined in it.
    
    Usage: python3 -I -B defined_check.py <script>
    
    A call's name is the word after a command substitution's opening, a dollar
    sign and a parenthesis, followed by one of the four names and a space,
    outside a comment line; a name is defined when a line of the script reads
    "<name>() {" (leading blanks allowed). The commands a script calls by name
    through them, "[", "cmp", "true" and "podman", are not helpers
    (gen/defined.py's list). Prints one line, "called <n>; undefined: <names or
    none>; yn defined: <yes|no|not called>; ynnot defined: ...; is defined:
    ...; isnot defined: ..."; exit 0 when no name is undefined and none of the
    four is called undefined, 1 otherwise, 2 on a usage or read error."""
    import re
    import sys
    
    COMMANDS = ("[", "cmp", "true", "podman")
    WRAPPERS = ("yn", "ynnot", "is", "isnot")
    CALL = re.compile(r"\$\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) ([^ )\"]+)")
    
    
    def main():
        if len(sys.argv) != 2:
            print("usage: defined_check.py <script>", file=sys.stderr)
            sys.exit(2)
        try:
            text = open(sys.argv[1], encoding="utf-8").read()
        except OSError as err:
            print("cannot read the script: %s" % err.strerror, file=sys.stderr)
            sys.exit(2)
        called, wrappers = set(), set()
        for line in text.split("\n"):
            if line.lstrip().startswith("#"):
                continue
            for wrapper, name in CALL.findall(line):
                wrappers.add(wrapper)
                called.add(name)
        defined = set(re.findall(r"^[ \t]*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\(\) \{", text, re.M))
        missing = sorted(n for n in called if n not in COMMANDS and n not in defined)
    
        def state(w):
            if w not in wrappers:
                return "not called"
            return "yes" if w in defined else "no"
        print("called %d; undefined: %s; %s"
              % (len(called), " ".join(missing) if missing else "none",
                 "; ".join("%s defined: %s" % (w, state(w)) for w in WRAPPERS)))
        bad = missing or any(state(w) == "no" for w in WRAPPERS)
        sys.exit(1 if bad else 0)
    
    
    main()
    PY
    echo "command: python3 -I -B <work>/defined_check.py <this script> (the program, written from this script's text, below; sha256 $(sha_of "$B/defined_check.py")), and the same over a copy of this script with one planted yn call and one planted is call of undefined helpers, and over a planted script that calls yn and is and defines neither (rulings Z, AD and AK a)"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/defined_check.py"
    python3 -I -B "$B/defined_check.py" "$SELF" >"$B/def-self.out" 2>"$B/def-self.err" </dev/null
    def_rc=$?
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/def-self.out"
    def_self_ok() { [ "$def_rc" = 0 ] && [ ! -s "$B/def-self.err" ] && [ "$(count_matches -F 'undefined: none; yn defined: yes; ynnot defined: yes; is defined: not called; isnot defined: not called' "$B/def-self.out")" = 1 ]; }
    check "every helper a yn or ynnot call of this script names is defined in it, yn and ynnot are themselves defined, and it calls neither is nor isnot (rulings Z, AD and AK a)" "$(yn def_self_ok)"
    { cat "$SELF"; printf '%s\n' "zz=\$""(yn zz_planted_undefined_helper)" "zi=\$""(is zz_planted_is_helper)"; } >"$B/def-plant.sh"
    python3 -I -B "$B/defined_check.py" "$B/def-plant.sh" >"$B/def-plant.out" 2>"$B/def-plant.err" </dev/null
    def_prc=$?
    echo "  over the planted copy: exit $def_prc; $(cat "$B/def-plant.out")"
    def_plant_ok() { [ "$def_prc" = 1 ] && [ "$(count_matches -F 'undefined: zz_planted_is_helper zz_planted_undefined_helper;' "$B/def-plant.out")" = 1 ] && [ "$(count_matches -F '; is defined: no;' "$B/def-plant.out")" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same check names the two planted undefined helpers in a copy of this script, the is call's among them, and is undefined there (rulings Z and AK a)" "$(yn def_plant_ok)"
    printf '%s\n' 'f() { :; }' "x=\$""(yn f)" "y=\$""(is f)" >"$B/def-noyn.sh"
    python3 -I -B "$B/defined_check.py" "$B/def-noyn.sh" >"$B/def-noyn.out" 2>"$B/def-noyn.err" </dev/null
    def_nrc=$?
    echo "  over a planted script defining f and calling yn f and is f: exit $def_nrc; $(cat "$B/def-noyn.out")"
    def_noyn_ok() { [ "$def_nrc" = 1 ] && [ "$(count_matches -F '; yn defined: no;' "$B/def-noyn.out")" = 1 ] && [ "$(count_matches -F '; is defined: no;' "$B/def-noyn.out")" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same check refuses a planted script that calls yn and is and defines neither (rulings AD and AK a)" "$(yn def_noyn_ok)"
    # P1 verification ruling D (change NXD): the placeholder check, the scan's
    # rule, over this script's own source, printed in this log with its
    # controls. A placeholder is a lower-case angle-bracketed word printed
    # immediately before a slash, or the target of a scrub; it is declared when
    # a root line says the word stands for something. The planted tokens are
    # built from pieces, so this text holds none.
    ph_used() {
      {
        LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E 's#[^#]*#<[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*>' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E '<[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*>$'
        LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E '<[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*>/' "$1" | sed 's#/$##'
      } | LC_ALL=C sort -u
    }
    ph_declared() {
      LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -E '(^|echo ")root: ' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E '<[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*>(/[a-z0-9]+)? stands for' |
        LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E '^<[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*>' | LC_ALL=C sort -u
    }
    ph_undeclared() { LC_ALL=C comm -23 <(ph_used "$1") <(ph_declared "$1") | count_lines /dev/stdin; }
    PL='<'
    { cat "$SELF"; printf '%s\n' "read ${PL}zzplanted>/x"; } >"$B/ph-plant.sh"
    { cat "$SELF"; printf '%s\n' "read ${PL}zzplanted>/x" "echo \"root: ${PL}zzplanted> stands for x\""; } >"$B/ph-decl.sh"
    { cat "$SELF"; printf '%s\n' "  sed -e \"s#\$X#${PL}zzscrub>#g\""; } >"$B/ph-scrub.sh"
    echo "command: the scan's placeholder rule (the tokens before a slash and the scrub targets, against the tokens the root lines declare) over this script, and over three planted copies of it: one printing a token before a slash, the same with a root line declaring it, one scrubbing to a token (P1 verification ruling D; change NXD)"
    echo "  this script: placeholders printed: $(ph_used "$SELF" | tr '\n' ' '); declared by root lines: $(ph_declared "$SELF" | tr '\n' ' '); undeclared: $(ph_undeclared "$SELF")"
    check "every placeholder this script prints is declared by a root line (the scan's rule; P1 verification ruling D; change NXD)" "$(yn [ "$(ph_undeclared "$SELF")" = 0 ])"
    echo "  the planted copies: undeclared $(ph_undeclared "$B/ph-plant.sh"), $(ph_undeclared "$B/ph-decl.sh") and $(ph_undeclared "$B/ph-scrub.sh")"
    check "control: the same check finds the one token a planted copy prints before a slash with no root line (change NXD)" "$(yn [ "$(ph_undeclared "$B/ph-plant.sh")" = 1 ])"
    check "control: the same check finds none when a root line in the planted copy declares it (change NXD)" "$(yn [ "$(ph_undeclared "$B/ph-decl.sh")" = 0 ])"
    check "control: the same check finds the scrub target a planted copy writes with no root line (change NXD)" "$(yn [ "$(ph_undeclared "$B/ph-scrub.sh")" = 1 ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the phase's commits by role, read from git"
    by_subject() { git log --format='%H' -n 1 -F --grep="$1"; }
    REC=$(by_subject "M6 part 1 P2 record: the logs, the run's records, the check, the scan")
    DOC=$(by_subject 'M6 part 1 P3: commit planning docs (the P2 verification and rulings)')
    PROBE=$(by_subject 'M6 part 1 P3: probe-emend-charts-write-xml gains add_chartsheet')
    CHANGELOG=$(by_subject 'M6 part 1 P3: the CHANGELOG names chartsheets')
    # Change NXK: the record the keep is compared with is the last committed
    # open-check record, the one P2's record commit, the base, added (no hash
    # is typed here); checked below to be an ancestor and the last. The corpus
    # run and P2's own fixture are compared with what P2's record commit names
    # (changes NXI and NXJ).
    PREV_OPEN_REC=$REC
    echo "command: git log --format=%H -n 1 -F --grep=<the role's subject>, for each role"
    echo "  P2's record commit (the base): ${REC:-none}"
    echo "  the doc commit: ${DOC:-none}"
    echo "  the probe commit: ${PROBE:-none}"
    echo "  the CHANGELOG commit, the phase commit: ${CHANGELOG:-none}"
    echo "  the record commit the keep is compared with (the last to add an open-check record; change NXK): ${PREV_OPEN_REC:-none}"
    echo "command: git rev-parse <phase commit>~0 to <phase commit>~3"
    for k in 0 1 2 3; do git rev-parse "$C~$k"; done | sed 's/^/    /'
    roles_in_order() {
      local r k=0
      for r in "$CHANGELOG" "$PROBE" "$DOC" "$REC"; do
        [ -n "$r" ] || return 1
        [ "$(git rev-parse "$C~$k")" = "$r" ] || return 1
        k=$((k + 1))
      done
    }
    check "the CHANGELOG commit, the probe commit, the doc commit and the base, each the next one's parent, the CHANGELOG commit the phase commit (change NXG)" "$(yn roles_in_order)"
    roles_ctl() { local CHANGELOG=$PROBE; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses the probe commit named as the phase commit (change NXG)" "$(ynnot roles_ctl)"
    roles_ctl2() { local REC=$DOC; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses the doc commit named as the base" "$(ynnot roles_ctl2)"
    roles_ctl3() { local PROBE=$DOC; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses the doc commit named as the probe commit (change NXG)" "$(ynnot roles_ctl3)"
    # record_is <commit> <subject prefix>: the commit is there, its subject
    # begins with the prefix, and it is an ancestor of the phase commit.
    record_is() { [ -n "$1" ] && git cat-file -e "$1^{commit}" && [ "$(git log -1 --format=%s "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -cE "^$2")" = 1 ] && git merge-base --is-ancestor "$1" "$C"; }
    echo "command: git log -1 --format=%s <P2's record commit>"
    echo "    $(git log -1 --format=%s "$PREV_OPEN_REC")"
    check "the named record commit is P2's record commit, an ancestor of the phase commit (change NXK)" "$(yn record_is "$PREV_OPEN_REC" 'M6 part 1 P2 record: ')"
    check "control: the same check refuses the doc commit named instead" "$(ynnot record_is "$DOC" 'M6 part 1 P2 record: ')"
    check "control: the same check refuses the probe commit named instead" "$(ynnot record_is "$PROBE" 'M6 part 1 P2 record: ')"
    # row_field <run.tsv> <column>: the run row's column, by header name.
    row_field() { awk -F'\t' -v c="$2" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == c) k = i; next } k && NR == 2 { print $k }' "$1"; }
    echo "  the phase commit given to this script: $C"
    echo "  git rev-parse HEAD at this run:        $(git rev-parse HEAD)"
    echo "  the controls' commits: the null commit $NULL_SHA; the fabricated commit $FAKE_SHA (the given one, its last hex digit changed); the short sha $SHORT"
    check "the phase commit given to this script is a full sha" "$(yn full_sha "$C")"
    check "the phase commit given to this script is HEAD" "$(yn head_is "$C")"
    check "the phase commit is the CHANGELOG commit, by its subject (change NXG)" "$(yn [ "$CHANGELOG" = "$C" ])"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the probe commit (change NXG)" "$(ynnot [ "$PROBE" = "$C" ])"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the null commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$NULL_SHA")"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses a fabricated commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$FAKE_SHA")"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses a short sha of the real commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$SHORT")"
    short_names_head() { [ "$(git rev-parse "$SHORT")" = "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" ]; }
    check "control: the short sha is the real commit's, so only its form is refused" "$(yn short_names_head)"
    echo "phase: Milestone 6 part 1 P3 ($SPEC) run.log; run at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    # Rulings AA and AK b (change NWV): every attempt refused at entry, or
    # superseded, is named by RERUN_NOTE and each of its files hashed here,
    # the hashing asserted by a check line (M5 part 6 P4's run log's form).
    # Change NXE (P1 verification ruling F): rerun_script <files>: some
    # file named is a .sh under <phase>/superseded, the superseded script that
    # wrote the attempt; its control runs every time.
    rerun_script() { local sf; for sf in $1; do case $sf in "$PHASE_DIR"/superseded/*.sh) return 0 ;; esac; done; return 1; }
    rerun_script_ctl() { ! rerun_script "$PHASE_DIR/superseded/x/run.log" && rerun_script "$PHASE_DIR/superseded/x/run.log $PHASE_DIR/superseded/x/m6p1-p3-run.sh"; }
    check "control: rerun_script refuses a planted RERUN_FILES naming a log alone, and takes one naming a script beside it (change NXE)" "$(yn rerun_script_ctl)"
    n_rerun_files=0
    n_rerun_missing=0
    if [ -n "${RERUN_NOTE:-}" ]; then
      echo "rerun: $RERUN_NOTE"
      echo "command: sha256sum and wc -c over each superseded attempt named above, with the directory it is kept in (ruling AA)"
      for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do
        n_rerun_files=$((n_rerun_files + 1))
        if [ -f "$sf" ]; then
          printf '    %s  %s bytes  %s  kept in %s\n' "$(sha256sum "$sf" | cut -d' ' -f1)" "$(wc -c <"$sf")" "$(basename "$sf")" "$(dirname "$sf")"
        else
          n_rerun_missing=$((n_rerun_missing + 1))
          printf '    NO HASH EXISTS for %s: the file is not there at run time (named in %s)\n' "$(basename "$sf")" "$(dirname "$sf")"
        fi
      done
      if [ -z "${RERUN_FILES:-}" ]; then echo "    RERUN_FILES was not set, so no attempt above is hashed by this run"; fi
      rerun_hashed() { [ "$n_rerun_files" -gt 0 ] && [ "$n_rerun_missing" = 0 ]; }
      check "every file of the attempt RERUN_NOTE names is hashed above, and RERUN_FILES names at least one (rulings AA and AK b)" "$(yn rerun_hashed)"
      # Change NWV: every file RERUN_FILES names lies in <phase>/superseded.
      rerun_kept() { local sf; for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do case $sf in "$PHASE_DIR"/superseded/*) ;; *) return 1 ;; esac; done; }
      check "every file RERUN_FILES names lies in <phase>/superseded (ruling AA)" "$(yn rerun_kept)"
      rerun_script_given() { rerun_script "${RERUN_FILES:-}"; }
      check "RERUN_FILES names the superseded script that wrote the attempt, a .sh under <phase>/superseded (P1 verification ruling F; change NXE)" "$(yn rerun_script_given)"
    fi
    
    # The two move checks as functions, run over planted inputs every time
    # below, and over a real moved keep or run directory when there is one.
    # keep_pairs_ok <listing>: the .in.xlsx lines times two equal the listing's
    # lines (the pattern in double quotes so the tab is interpolated).
    keep_pairs_ok() {
      local pairs files
      pairs=$(count_matches -E "[.]in[.]xlsx${TAB}" "$1")
      files=$(count_lines "$1")
      [ "$files" -ge 2 ] && [ "$((pairs * 2))" = "$files" ]
    }
    # run_listing <dir> <listing>: the listing of a run directory, one line per
    # file, path and bytes.
    run_listing() { (cd "$1" && find . -type f -printf '%P\t%s\n' | LC_ALL=C sort) >"$2"; }
    # run_listing_ok <dir> <listing>: the listing names each file once and at
    # least one.
    run_listing_ok() {
      local files lines uniq
      files=$(find "$1" -type f | wc -l)
      lines=$(count_lines "$2")
      uniq=$(cut -f1 "$2" | LC_ALL=C sort -u | count_lines /dev/stdin)
      [ "$files" -ge 1 ] && [ "$lines" = "$files" ] && [ "$uniq" = "$files" ]
    }
    
    if [ -n "$SUPERSEDED_RUN" ]; then
    for SUP_S in $SAMPLES; do
      SUP_OUT=$RUN_OUT_ROOT/$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SUP_S
      SUP_TO=$SELF_DIR/out/superseded/run-$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SUP_S
      echo "the superseded run directory, moved before this run: <runs>/$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SUP_S to <scripts>/out/superseded/run-$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SUP_S"
      sup_there=no
      if [ -d "$SUP_OUT" ]; then
        sup_there=yes
        echo "command: sha256sum <runs>/$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SUP_S/summary.host.tsv and summary.i686.tsv; mv <runs>/$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SUP_S <scripts>/out/superseded/run-$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SUP_S"
        for sl in host i686; do
          if [ -f "$SUP_OUT/summary.$sl.tsv" ]; then echo "    summary.$sl.tsv sha256 $(sha_of "$SUP_OUT/summary.$sl.tsv")"; else echo "    summary.$sl.tsv: NO HASH EXISTS, the file is not there"; fi
        done
        run_listing "$SUP_OUT" "$B/superseded-run.listing"
        echo "command: (cd <runs>/$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SUP_S && find . -type f -printf '%P<tab>%s<newline>' | LC_ALL=C sort) | sha256sum"
        echo "    files $(find "$SUP_OUT" -type f | wc -l); listing lines $(count_lines "$B/superseded-run.listing"); listing sha256 $(sha_of "$B/superseded-run.listing")"
        check "the listing of $SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SUP_S names each of its files once" "$(yn run_listing_ok "$SUP_OUT" "$B/superseded-run.listing")"
        if [ -e "$SUP_TO" ]; then echo "    $SUP_TO is already there"; fail=1; else mkdir -p "$SELF_DIR/out/superseded" && mv "$SUP_OUT" "$SUP_TO"; fi
      fi
      sup_moved() { [ ! -e "$SUP_OUT" ] && [ -d "$SUP_TO" ]; }
      if [ "$sup_there" = yes ]; then
        check "the superseded run directory $SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SUP_S is moved, not removed, before the run" "$(yn sup_moved)"
      else
        echo "    <runs>/$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SUP_S was not there; nothing to move (P3's NTT, carried; change NUB)"
      fi
    done
    fi
    if [ -n "$SUPERSEDED_KEEP" ]; then
      KEEP_TO=$SELF_DIR/out/superseded/keep-$SUPERSEDED_KEEP
      echo "the superseded keep, moved before this run: <keep> to <scripts>/out/superseded/keep-$SUPERSEDED_KEEP"
      if [ -d "$KEEP" ]; then
        (cd "$KEEP" && find . -type f -printf '%P\t%s\n' | LC_ALL=C sort) >"$B/superseded-keep.listing"
        echo "command: (cd <keep> && find . -type f -printf '%P<tab>%s<newline>' | LC_ALL=C sort) | sha256sum; the .in.xlsx files counted; mv <keep> <scripts>/out/superseded/keep-$SUPERSEDED_KEEP"
        echo "    pairs $(count_matches -E "[.]in[.]xlsx${TAB}" "$B/superseded-keep.listing"); files $(count_lines "$B/superseded-keep.listing"); listing sha256 $(sha_of "$B/superseded-keep.listing")"
        check "the moved keep's pairs times two equals its files" "$(yn keep_pairs_ok "$B/superseded-keep.listing")"
        if [ -e "$KEEP_TO" ]; then echo "    $KEEP_TO is already there"; fail=1; else mkdir -p "$SELF_DIR/out/superseded" && mv "$KEEP" "$KEEP_TO"; fi
      else
        echo "    NO LISTING EXISTS: there is no keep in place to move"
      fi
      keep_moved() { [ ! -e "$KEEP" ] && [ -d "$KEEP_TO" ]; }
      check "the superseded keep is moved, not removed, before the run" "$(yn keep_moved)"
    fi
    echo "superseded run directory named: ${SUPERSEDED_RUN:-none}; superseded keep named: ${SUPERSEDED_KEEP:-none}"
    echo
    echo "## the two move checks over planted inputs, run every time"
    printf 'x.1.in.xlsx%s1\nx.1.out.xlsx%s1\n' "$TAB" "$TAB" >"$B/c-keep.listing"
    printf 'x.1.in.xlsx%s1\nx.1.out.xlsx%s1\ny.1.out.xlsx%s1\n' "$TAB" "$TAB" "$TAB" >"$B/c-keep-odd.listing"
    echo "  planted keep listing: pairs $(count_matches -E "[.]in[.]xlsx${TAB}" "$B/c-keep.listing"), files $(count_lines "$B/c-keep.listing"); with an unpaired output: pairs $(count_matches -E "[.]in[.]xlsx${TAB}" "$B/c-keep-odd.listing"), files $(count_lines "$B/c-keep-odd.listing")"
    check "keep_pairs_ok passes a planted listing of one whole pair" "$(yn keep_pairs_ok "$B/c-keep.listing")"
    check "control: keep_pairs_ok refuses a planted listing with an unpaired output" "$(ynnot keep_pairs_ok "$B/c-keep-odd.listing")"
    mkdir -p "$B/c-run/abc123" && printf 'a' >"$B/c-run/summary.host.tsv" && printf 'bb' >"$B/c-run/abc123/out.host.xlsx" && printf 'ccc' >"$B/c-run/abc123/stdout.host.txt"
    run_listing "$B/c-run" "$B/c-run.listing"
    echo "  planted run directory: files $(find "$B/c-run" -type f | wc -l); listing lines $(count_lines "$B/c-run.listing"); listing sha256 $(sha_of "$B/c-run.listing")"
    check "run_listing_ok passes the planted run directory's own listing" "$(yn run_listing_ok "$B/c-run" "$B/c-run.listing")"
    { cat "$B/c-run.listing"; head -n 1 "$B/c-run.listing"; } >"$B/c-run-dup.listing"
    check "control: run_listing_ok refuses a listing that names one file twice" "$(ynnot run_listing_ok "$B/c-run" "$B/c-run-dup.listing")"
    n_cargo=$(pgrep -x cargo | wc -l)
    n_rustc=$(pgrep -x rustc | wc -l)
    echo "SERIALIZED: no other log run was in flight; cargo processes at entry: $n_cargo; rustc processes at entry: $n_rustc; this run builds into <target>/main, the main tree's subdirectory of the phase's target root (CARGO_TARGET_DIR; change NSU)"
    no_build_running() { [ "$((n_cargo + n_rustc))" = 0 ]; }
    check "no cargo or rustc process was running at entry" "$(yn no_build_running)"
    echo "DETACHED: no interactive call waits on this run; stdout and stderr go to a file, polled from later calls."
    echo "TIMEOUT CHOSEN BEFORE THE RUN: --timeout 300 for the sample's child and --lo-timeout $LO_TIMEOUT_S per conversion, the figures every corpus run since Milestone 3 used; not tuned during the run."
    echo "root: <repo> stands for the repository's top level (inside <home>, scrubbed after <runs> and <corpus>, whose paths begin with it); scripts/counting.sh is read from it at the phase commit by git show; scripts/passthrough-run.sh, scripts/passthrough-record.py and scripts/edit-open-check.sh are run from it, each checked equal to the phase commit's, and the runner and the open check each source scripts/lo-check.sh, which is never run; scripts/openpyxl-ops.py and tests/fixtures/openpyxl-ops.xlsx are mounted read-only from it into the openpyxl image, each checked equal to the phase commit's (change NXC); the keep's tests run in it; the two record pairs are installed into its $RECORDS_DEST/"
    echo "root: <home> stands for the home directory of the account that ran this script"
    echo "root: <phase> stands for <home>/.cache/emend-build/m6p1-p3 on the disk, the phase's directory; a superseded attempt's files are kept in <phase>/superseded; the size log is read from <phase>/logs/size.log unless the second argument names another (change NXH)"
    echo "root: <p2phase> stands for <home>/.cache/emend-build/m6p1-p2 on the disk, P2's phase directory, read only: P2's run kept its working directory under <p2phase>/tmp (change NXJ)"
    echo "root: <p2work> stands for the one directory under <p2phase>/tmp holding the openpyxl op output P2's run.log hashed, P2's run's kept working directory, read only (change NXJ)"
    echo "root: <sizebuild> stands for the size log's build directory, <target>/main unless SIZE_BUILD_ROOT names another for a dry run; its four release binaries are copied into <work>/bin, never run from it (change NXH)"
    echo "root: <scratch> stands for <phase>, the phase's directory, named <scratch> where TMPDIR is concerned as the close-out's scripts name it: TMPDIR is <scratch>/tmp, made and exported by this script before any mktemp, and <work> is made under it (close-out ruling 1; change NTI)"
    echo "root: <scripts> stands for <phase>/scripts on the disk, this script's own directory, which holds the script alone (change NVO); the two record pairs are written into <scripts>/out/records first (a dry run's into RECORDS_DEST/staged: change NWS), a superseded run directory and a superseded keep are moved into <scripts>/out/superseded, and this script's own standard error goes to <scripts>/out/run.stderr (specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7)"
    echo "root: <work> stands for this run's working directory, made by mktemp -d under TMPDIR, <scratch>/tmp, on the disk (change NTI; the counting library, the checks' programs and outputs, derived tables, the planted listings, run directory and entry rows, the runs' TMPDIR <work>/tmp-run, the open check's TMPDIR <work>/tmp, the earlier-run and placeholder controls, the size log's four release binaries copied into <work>/bin/host and <work>/bin/i686 (change NXH), the openpyxl fixture's output directory <work>/opx, its corpus <work>/opxcorpus, the charts sample's run directory <work>/opxrun-charts and the refused sample's output directory <work>/opx-refused, and P2's fixture's corpus copied into <work>/p2opxcorpus, its charts run directory <work>/p2opxrun-charts and its refused sample's output directory <work>/p2opx-refused: changes NXB to NXD, NXH and NXJ), kept after the run and never removed"
    echo "root: <target> stands for <phase>/target on the disk, the phase's one target root: this log builds the keep's tests of <repo> into <target>/main, the main tree's subdirectory, and into no other; it builds no release binary, the size log having built them there (changes NSK and NXH)"
    echo "root: <keep> stands for <phase>/keep-host on the disk unless RUN_KEEP names another for a dry run, this phase's host keep; kept after the run for planning"
    echo "root: <corpus> stands for the private corpus directory (the manifest and the inputs under <corpus>/corpus, read)"
    echo "root: <runs> stands for the corpus run directories' parent, <corpus>/runs unless RUN_OUT_ROOT names another for a dry run; this log's run directory <runs>/$RUN-chartsheet is written there; P2's run directory, the one the record P2's record commit added names, is read from <corpus>/runs and never written (change NXI)"
    apart() { case "$1/" in "$2"/*) return 1 ;; esac; case "$2/" in "$1"/*) return 1 ;; esac; return 0; }
    roots_distinct() {
      local a b all=("$SELF_DIR" "$BUILD_ROOT" "$MAIN" "$KEEP" "$CORPUS" "$TMPDIR")
      for a in "${all[@]}"; do for b in "${all[@]}"; do
        [ "$a" = "$b" ] && continue
        apart "$a" "$b" || return 1
      done; done
    }
    check "the roots other than <home>, <phase>, <work> and <runs> are distinct, none inside another (TMPDIR, <scratch>/tmp, among them; change NTI)" "$(yn roots_distinct)"
    work_in_tmpdir() { case "$B/" in "$TMPDIR/"*) return 0 ;; esac; return 1; }
    check "<work>, the directory mktemp -d made, is under TMPDIR, <scratch>/tmp (close-out ruling 1; change NTI)" "$(yn work_in_tmpdir)"
    work_ctl() { local B=/tmp/x; work_in_tmpdir; }
    check "control: the same test refuses a working directory under /tmp" "$(ynnot work_ctl)"
    work_ctl2() { local B=$SELF_DIR/out/work.x; work_in_tmpdir; }
    check "control: the same test refuses one under <scripts>/out, where the carried form made it" "$(ynnot work_ctl2)"
    tmpdir_ctl() { local TMPDIR=$SELF_DIR/out; work_in_tmpdir; }
    check "control: the same test refuses <work> against a TMPDIR it is not under" "$(ynnot tmpdir_ctl)"
    # Change NTS (specs/0033 "Planning rulings on P1", ruling 12): every
    # mktemp call of this script is checked under TMPDIR, so the source is
    # read for its calls outside comments; the call's text is built from
    # pieces, so this form's own text is no call.
    MKW='$('
    MKW=${MKW}mkt
    MKW=${MKW}emp
    count_tempcalls() {
      awk -v w="$MKW" '{ l = $0; sub(/^[ \t]+/, "", l); if (substr(l, 1, 1) == "#") next; s = l
        while ((i = index(s, w)) > 0) { n++; s = substr(s, i + length(w)) }
      } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"
    }
    printf '%s\n' "A=$MKW -d)" "F=$MKW)" "# $MKW -d)" >"$B/mktemp-fixture"
    n_mk=$(count_tempcalls "$SELF")
    n_mk_fix=$(count_tempcalls "$B/mktemp-fixture")
    echo "command: count_tempcalls <this script>, and the same over a fixture of three lines: a directory call, a file call, a comment"
    echo "  mktemp calls in this script outside comments: $n_mk (the one that makes <work>, checked under TMPDIR above); in the fixture: $n_mk_fix"
    check "this script makes one mktemp call, <work>'s, and no plain temporary file (ruling 12; change NTS)" "$(yn [ "$n_mk" = 1 ])"
    check "control: the same count finds the fixture's two calls and not its comment" "$(yn [ "$n_mk_fix" = 2 ])"
    runs_apart() { apart "$RUN_OUT_ROOT" "$MAIN" && apart "$RUN_OUT_ROOT" "$SELF_DIR"; }
    check "<runs> lies outside <repo> and <scripts>" "$(yn runs_apart)"
    check "control: apart refuses <target>/main/release against <target>/main, which holds it" "$(ynnot apart "$BUILD_ROOT/release" "$BUILD_ROOT")"
    echo "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set in this shell: $([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    key_unset() { [ -z "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ]; }
    check "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not set" "$(yn key_unset)"
    key_set_ctl() { local ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=planted; key_unset; }
    check "control: the same check refuses a shell where the variable is set" "$(ynnot key_set_ctl)"
    echo "the run directories: $(for s in $SAMPLES; do printf '<runs>/%s-%s ' "$RUN" "$s"; done)(change NVX)"
    echo "the record stems: ${STEMS[chartsheet]} and $STEM_OPEN; the records' destination: $RECORDS_DEST; RUN_SKIP_KEEP: $RUN_SKIP_KEEP"
    echo "at entry: status lines $entry_all; of them admitted by the phase's pattern (this phase's logs, its two record pairs, the API and size records, planning's modified specs/0038 and ROADMAP.md) $entry_ours; the lines:"
    git status --porcelain | sed 's/^/    /'
    ours_ctl() { printf ' M scripts/check.sh\n' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE "$OURS"; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern refuses a modified gate file" "$(ynnot ours_ctl)"
    ours_rec_ctl() { printf '?? records/logs/m6p1-p3/run.log\n?? records/logs/m6p1-p2/run.log\n?? records/m6p1-p3-chartsheet-%s-%s.md\n?? records/m6p1-open-%s-%s.txt\n?? records/m6p1-p3-chartsheet-%s-abcdef0.md\n?? records/m6p1-p3-%s-%s.md\n?? records/m6p1-p2-%s-%s.md\n?? records/api-review-m6p1-2026-01-01-%s.md\n?? records/size-m6p1-%s-%s.md\n?? records/size-m6p1-%s-abcdef0.md\n?? records/api-review-m5p6-%s-%s.md\n?? records/logs/m6p1-p3x/run.log\n M ROADMAP.md\n M specs/0038-chartsheets.md\n M specs/0037-measurement-and-close.md\n M records/m6p1-p3-chartsheet-%s-%s.md\n M crates/emend/src/package.rs\n M records/size-m6p1-%s-%s.md\n' "$DATE" "$SHORT" "$DATE" "$SHORT" "$DATE" "$DATE" "$SHORT" "$DATE" "$SHORT" "$SHORT" "$DATE" "$SHORT" "$DATE" "$DATE" "$SHORT" "$DATE" "$SHORT" "$DATE" "$SHORT" | count_matches -E "$OURS" /dev/stdin; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern admits this phase's log, its two untracked record pairs, an untracked API record and size record of the phase commit and planning's modified specs/0038 and ROADMAP.md alone; it refuses another phase's log, a record of another commit, a stem without the sample word, P2's record stem, a size record of another commit, another part's API record, a sibling directory, specs/0037, a modified record, a source file and a modified size record (changes NSB, NUI and NXG)" "$(yn [ "$(ours_rec_ctl)" = 7 ])"
    echo
    echo "## script that wrote this log"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$SELF"
    echo
    echo "## the shared counting library this log sources (the phase commit's, by git show; change NSB)"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/counting.sh"
    echo
    echo "## counting controls"
    counting_controls
    if [ "$counting_controls_ok" != yes ]; then fail=1; fi
    
    echo
    echo "## the scripts, against the phase commit, and planning's uncommitted spec"
    tree_is_commit() { [ "$(sha_of "$1")" = "$(git show "$C:$1" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" ]; }
    for s in scripts/passthrough-run.sh scripts/passthrough-record.py scripts/lo-check.sh scripts/edit-open-check.sh scripts/openpyxl-ops.py tests/fixtures/openpyxl-ops.xlsx; do
      check "$s in the main tree is the phase commit's (sha256 $(sha_of "$s"))" "$(yn tree_is_commit "$s")"
    done
    tree_ctl() { [ "$(git show "$C:scripts/excel-check-list.py" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" = "$(sha_of scripts/edit-open-check.sh)" ]; }
    check "control: the same hash comparison tells two different scripts apart" "$(ynnot tree_ctl)"
    spec_now=$(sha_of "$SPEC")
    spec_committed=$(git show "$C:$SPEC" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    spec_doc=$(git show "$DOC:$SPEC" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:$SPEC | sha256sum; git show <doc commit>:$SPEC | sha256sum; sha256sum $SPEC (the working file: should planning hold a ruling during P3 uncommitted, checked against PLANNING_SPEC when it is given; change NXG)"
    echo "  at the phase commit: $spec_committed; at the doc commit: $spec_doc; the pin: $SPEC_WANT"
    echo "  the working tree's copy (planning's uncommitted rulings): sha256 $spec_now"
    spec_ok() { [ "$spec_committed" = "$SPEC_WANT" ]; }
    check "the spec at the phase commit is at the pinned hash" "$(yn spec_ok)"
    check "the spec at the phase commit is the doc commit's" "$(yn [ "$spec_committed" = "$spec_doc" ])"
    spec_ctl() { local spec_committed=1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111; spec_ok; }
    check "control: the same check refuses the spec against another hash" "$(ynnot spec_ctl)"
    echo "  PLANNING_SPEC: ${PLANNING_SPEC:-unset}"
    planning_spec_ok() { [ -z "$PLANNING_SPEC" ] || [ "$spec_now" = "$PLANNING_SPEC" ]; }
    check "the working copy of the spec is at PLANNING_SPEC when it is given (change NWS)" "$(yn planning_spec_ok)"
    planning_spec_ctl() { local PLANNING_SPEC=1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111; planning_spec_ok; }
    check "control: the same check refuses a working copy against another hash" "$(ynnot planning_spec_ctl)"
    echo "command: podman image exists $IMAGE"
    check "the pinned LibreOffice image is there" "$(yn podman image exists "$IMAGE")"
    
    echo
    echo "## the release binaries: the size log's, copied into <work>/bin and checked against size.log's lines, both targets, for every run below (specs/0038 \"P3\": the P2 runs rerun with the size log's release binaries; M5 part 6 P3's changes NWA and NWQ, their form; change NXH)"
    echo "input: the size log: $SIZE_LOG (the second argument, or <phase>/logs/size.log; change NXH)"
    echo "input (environment) SIZE_BUILD_ROOT: ${INPUT_SEEN[SIZE_BUILD_ROOT]} (unset: the size log's build directory is <target>/main; a dry run may name another; change NXH)"
    size_log_there() { [ -s "$SIZE_LOG" ]; }
    check "the size log is there and not empty" "$(yn size_log_there)"
    echo "command: sha256sum <the size log>: $(sha_of "$SIZE_LOG" 2>/dev/null); tail -n 1 <the size log>: $(tail -n 1 "$SIZE_LOG" 2>/dev/null)"
    SIZE_LAST='size log checks all as expected: yes'
    size_log_passed() { [ "$(tail -n 1 "$SIZE_LOG" 2>/dev/null)" = "$SIZE_LAST" ]; }
    check "the size log's last line is \"$SIZE_LAST\" (change NXH)" "$(yn size_log_passed)"
    printf 'x\nsize log checks all as expected: no\n' >"$B/c-size-last.log"
    size_last_ctl() { local SIZE_LOG=$B/c-size-last.log; size_log_passed; }
    check "control: the same check refuses a planted log ending \"size log checks all as expected: no\"" "$(ynnot size_last_ctl)"
    # The size log prints each release binary it builds as two spaces, its path
    # under <target>/main (the host's release directory, or the i686 triple's),
    # ": sha256 ", 64 hex, ", bytes " and a count: M4 part 2 P2's form for its
    # host emend-copy (records/logs/m4p2-p2/size.log).
    HASH_FORM='^  <target>/main/(i686-unknown-linux-musl/)?release/(emend-copy|xlsx-diff): sha256 [0-9a-f]{64}, bytes [0-9]+$'
    n_hash=$(count_matches -E "$HASH_FORM" "$SIZE_LOG")
    echo "command: count_matches -E <the release hash line form> <the size log>: $n_hash"
    check "size.log holds exactly four release hash lines: emend-copy and xlsx-diff, host and $I686" "$(yn [ "$n_hash" = 4 ])"
    # sized_of <log> <triple path or nothing> <binary>: the hash the log prints
    # for that binary, or nothing.
    sized_of() { sed -n -E "s#^  <target>/main/$2release/$3: sha256 ([0-9a-f]{64}), bytes [0-9]+\$#\1#p" "$1" | head -n 1; }
    printf '  <target>/main/release/emend-copy: sha256 %s, bytes 1\n  <target>/main/%s/release/emend-copy: sha256 %s, bytes 1\n' \
      "$(printf 'a' | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" "$I686" "$(printf 'b' | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" >"$B/c-size.log"
    sized_ctl() { [ "$(sized_of "$B/c-size.log" "" emend-copy)" = "$(printf 'a' | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" ] && [ "$(sized_of "$B/c-size.log" "$I686/" emend-copy)" = "$(printf 'b' | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" ]; }
    check "control: sized_of tells the host line from the $I686 line in a planted log holding both" "$(yn sized_ctl)"
    check "control: the same form counts two lines in that planted log" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -E "$HASH_FORM" "$B/c-size.log")" = 2 ])"
    mkdir -p "$B/bin/host" "$B/bin/i686" || exit 2
    n_bin_ok=0
    for label in host i686; do
      if [ "$label" = i686 ]; then tp="$I686/"; else tp=""; fi
      for bin in emend-copy xlsx-diff; do
        src=$SIZE_BUILD/${tp}release/$bin
        cp "$src" "$B/bin/$label/$bin"
        want=$(sized_of "$SIZE_LOG" "$tp" "$bin")
        have=$(sha_of "$B/bin/$label/$bin")
        echo "command: cp <sizebuild>/${tp}release/$bin <work>/bin/$label/$bin"
        echo "  <work>/bin/$label/$bin: sha256 $have, bytes $(stat -c %s "$B/bin/$label/$bin"); size.log's line: ${want:-none}"
        bin_is_sized() { [ -n "$want" ] && [ "$have" = "$want" ]; }
        if bin_is_sized; then n_bin_ok=$((n_bin_ok + 1)); fi
        check "$label $bin: the copy is the binary size.log hashed, not a rebuild" "$(yn bin_is_sized)"
      done
    done
    check "the four copies are the four binaries size.log hashed ($n_bin_ok of 4)" "$(yn [ "$n_bin_ok" = 4 ])"
    bin_ctl() { local have; have=$(printf 'x' | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1); bin_is_sized; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses another hash" "$(ynnot bin_ctl)"
    PT_host=$B/bin/host/emend-copy
    XD_host=$B/bin/host/xlsx-diff
    PT_i686=$B/bin/i686/emend-copy
    XD_i686=$B/bin/i686/xlsx-diff
    echo "  this log builds no release binary; every run below uses these four copies (change NXH); $(rustc --version)"
    
    echo
    echo "## the corpus manifest, and its workbooks holding a calculation chain (specs/0025 P3 verification ruling 4; change NSI)"
    awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next } { print $k["id"] "\t" $k["ext"] }' "$CORPUS/manifest.tsv" >"$B/order"
    manifest_rows=$(count_lines "$B/order")
    n_regular=$(find "$CORPUS/corpus" -maxdepth 1 -type f | wc -l)
    echo "command: awk over <corpus>/manifest.tsv's id and ext columns by header name; find <corpus>/corpus -maxdepth 1 -type f"
    echo "  manifest rows: $manifest_rows; regular files under <corpus>/corpus: $n_regular"
    check "the manifest names one workbook per regular file of the corpus directory" "$(yn [ "$manifest_rows" = "$n_regular" ])"
    check "the manifest names some workbook" "$(yn [ "$manifest_rows" -ge 1 ])"
    : >"$B/chain-ids"
    while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
      if [ "$(python3 -I -B -c 'import sys, zipfile; print(1 if "xl/calcChain.xml" in zipfile.ZipFile(sys.argv[1]).namelist() else 0)' "$CORPUS/corpus/$id.$ext")" = 1 ]; then
        printf '%s\n' "$id" >>"$B/chain-ids"
      fi
    done <"$B/order"
    N_CHAIN=$(count_lines "$B/chain-ids")
    echo "command: python3 -I -B -c <zipfile namelist> <corpus>/corpus/<id>.<ext>, for each manifest row"
    echo "  corpus workbooks holding xl/calcChain.xml: $N_CHAIN of $manifest_rows (ids: $(paste -sd' ' "$B/chain-ids"))"
    echo "  the rule covering them (change NSI): the sample writes no cell, so each calcChain entry is identical and unflagged on both labels, and none is dropped"
    check "some corpus workbook holds a calculation chain, so the chain rows below are read" "$(yn [ "$N_CHAIN" -ge 1 ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the chartsheet sample's line and entry rules, with their controls (specs/0038 \"Harness runs\"; change NWW)"
    kv() { printf '%s\n' "$1" | tr '\t ' '\n\n' | sed -n "s/^$2=//p" | head -1; }
    # The tool's keys, in its order (tools/emend-copy, --chartsheet-sample).
    KEYS_chartsheet="part_length charts series sheets_after kept_charts"
    echo "  the chartsheet sample's keys, in the tool's order: $KEYS_chartsheet"
    # keys_ok <word> <keys> <tool line>: the word, then the keys in the tool's
    # order, each a number.
    keys_ok() {
      local k v got
      got=$(printf '%s\n' "$3" | tr '\t' '\n' | sed -n '2,$s/=.*//p' | paste -sd' ')
      [ "$(printf '%s\n' "$3" | cut -f1)" = "$1" ] || return 1
      [ "$got" = "$2" ] || return 1
      for k in $2; do
        v=$(kv "$3" "$k")
        printf '%s' "$v" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qxE '[0-9]+' || return 1
      done
    }
    # chartsheet_line_ok <tool line> <input sheets> <added name length>
    # <kept charts>: what "Harness runs" asks of the line: one chart of two
    # series on the new part, the sheet list one longer than the input's, the
    # part name's length the added chartsheet entry's, and the input's
    # chartsheets' charts the count given (change NWW).
    chartsheet_line_ok() {
      keys_ok chartsheet "$KEYS_chartsheet" "$1" || return 1
      printf '%s' "$2" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qxE '[0-9]+' || return 1
      [ "$(kv "$1" charts)" = 1 ] || return 1
      [ "$(kv "$1" series)" = 2 ] || return 1
      [ "$(kv "$1" sheets_after)" = "$(($2 + 1))" ] || return 1
      [ "$(kv "$1" part_length)" = "$3" ] || return 1
      [ "$(kv "$1" kept_charts)" = "$4" ]
    }
    # The tool test's line (tools/emend-copy/tests/null_rewrite.rs).
    LINE_C=$(printf 'chartsheet\tpart_length=25\tcharts=1\tseries=2\tsheets_after=2\tkept_charts=0')
    echo "  the tool test's line: $(printf '%s' "$LINE_C" | tr '\t' ' ')"
    check "control: chartsheet_line_ok accepts the tool test's line for one input sheet and a 25-byte name" "$(yn chartsheet_line_ok "$LINE_C" 1 25 0)"
    check "control: chartsheet_line_ok refuses the same line read for two input sheets" "$(ynnot chartsheet_line_ok "$LINE_C" 2 25 0)"
    check "control: chartsheet_line_ok refuses the same line read for a 26-byte name" "$(ynnot chartsheet_line_ok "$LINE_C" 1 26 0)"
    check "control: chartsheet_line_ok refuses the same line read with one kept chart" "$(ynnot chartsheet_line_ok "$LINE_C" 1 25 1)"
    check "control: chartsheet_line_ok refuses the line with two charts" "$(ynnot chartsheet_line_ok "$(printf '%s' "$LINE_C" | sed 's/charts=1/charts=2/')" 1 25 0)"
    check "control: chartsheet_line_ok refuses the line with one series" "$(ynnot chartsheet_line_ok "$(printf '%s' "$LINE_C" | sed 's/series=2/series=1/')" 1 25 0)"
    check "control: chartsheet_line_ok refuses the line with a key missing" "$(ynnot chartsheet_line_ok "$(printf '%s' "$LINE_C" | sed 's/\tseries=2//')" 1 25 0)"
    check "control: chartsheet_line_ok refuses the keys out of the tool's order" "$(ynnot chartsheet_line_ok "$(printf '%s\tseries=2' "$(printf '%s' "$LINE_C" | sed 's/\tseries=2//')")" 1 25 0)"
    check "control: chartsheet_line_ok refuses the add-chart sample's word" "$(ynnot chartsheet_line_ok "$(printf '%s' "$LINE_C" | sed 's/^chartsheet/addchart/')" 1 25 0)"
    check "control: chartsheet_line_ok refuses an input sheet count that is not a number" "$(ynnot chartsheet_line_ok "$LINE_C" error 25 0)"
    check "control: chartsheet_line_ok refuses a value that is not a number" "$(ynnot chartsheet_line_ok "$(printf '%s' "$LINE_C" | sed 's/kept_charts=0/kept_charts=x/')" 1 25 0)"
    # P1's summary helpers, carried verbatim (part 4 P2's change NVA, carried).
    count_where() { awk -F'\t' -v c="$2" -v v="$3" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == c) k = i; next } k && $k == v { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    # count_ok_where <summary> <column> <value>: among the rows whose outcome is ok.
    count_ok_where() { awk -F'\t' -v c="$2" -v v="$3" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) { if ($i == c) k = i; if ($i == "outcome") o = i }; next } k && o && $o == "ok" && $k == v { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    sum_col() { awk -F'\t' -v c="$2" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == c) k = i; next } k { n += $k } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    # status_rows <entries> <status>: the entry rows of that status, every
    # workbook.
    status_rows() { awk -F'\t' -v s="$2" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == "status") k = i; next } k && $k == s { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    # added_chartsheet <entries> <id>: the added chartsheet entry's name, the one
    # row named chartsheets/sheet<N>.xml in some directory, not a rels part,
    # or nothing.
    added_chartsheet() {
      awk -F'\t' -v id="$2" '
        NR == 1 { for (c = 1; c <= NF; c++) k[$c] = c; next }
        $k["id"] == id && $k["status"] == "added" && $k["name"] ~ /^([^\/]+\/)*chartsheets\/sheet[0-9]+[.]xml$/ { n++; nm = $k["name"] }
        END { if (n == 1) print nm }' "$1"
    }
    # chartsheet_named <entries> <id>: the runner's rows for one workbook as
    # "Harness runs" gives them for the chartsheet sample (change NWW): three
    # changed, [Content_Types].xml, the workbook part (an .xml entry at the top
    # of a directory, outside any _rels) and that part's rels part, the
    # workbook's own and no other; five added, unflagged: the chartsheet and
    # its rels part beside the workbook part (chartsheets/sheet<N>.xml and
    # chartsheets/_rels/sheet<N>.xml.rels in the workbook part's directory,
    # the one N), the drawing
    # and its rels part (xl/drawings/drawing<M>.xml and its rels, the one M)
    # and one chart part xl/charts/chart<K>.xml; every other row identical and
    # unflagged; nothing dropped or recompressed. A changed row may carry the
    # runner's flags, its local header rewritten.
    chartsheet_named() {
      awk -F'\t' -v id="$2" '
        NR == 1 { for (c = 1; c <= NF; c++) k[$c] = c; next }
        $k["id"] != id { next }
        {
          n++; s = $k["status"]; f = $k["flags"]; nm = $k["name"]
          if (s == "identical") { if (f != "") bad++; next }
          if (s == "added") {
            if (f != "") bad++
            if (nm ~ /^([^\/]+\/)*chartsheets\/sheet[0-9]+[.]xml$/) { cs++; csn = nm }
            else if (nm ~ /^([^\/]+\/)*chartsheets\/_rels\/sheet[0-9]+[.]xml[.]rels$/) { csr++; csrn = nm }
            else if (nm ~ /^xl\/drawings\/drawing[0-9]+[.]xml$/) { dr++; drn = nm }
            else if (nm ~ /^xl\/drawings\/_rels\/drawing[0-9]+[.]xml[.]rels$/) { drr++; drrn = nm }
            else if (nm ~ /^xl\/charts\/chart[0-9]+[.]xml$/) chart++
            else bad++
            next
          }
          if (s == "changed") {
            if (nm == "[Content_Types].xml") ct++
            else if (nm ~ /\/_rels\/[^\/]+[.]xml[.]rels$/) { wbr++; wbrn = nm }
            else if (nm ~ /^([^\/]+\/)*[^\/]+[.]xml$/) { wb++; wbn = nm }
            else bad++
            next
          }
          bad++
        }
        END {
          if (n == 0 || bad > 0 || ct != 1 || wb != 1 || wbr != 1 || cs != 1 || csr != 1 || dr != 1 || drr != 1 || chart != 1) exit 1
          # The rels part belongs to the workbook part: _rels/<name>.rels in its
          # directory.
          d = wbn; sub(/[^\/]+$/, "", d); b = substr(wbn, length(d) + 1)
          if (wbrn != d "_rels/" b ".rels") exit 1
          # The chartsheet beside the workbook part, its rels part its own.
          if (substr(csn, 1, length(d) + 12) != d "chartsheets/") exit 1
          c = csn; sub(/^.*\//, "", c)
          if (csrn != d "chartsheets/_rels/" c ".rels") exit 1
          e = drn; sub(/^.*\//, "", e)
          if (drrn != "xl/drawings/_rels/" e ".rels") exit 1
        }' "$1"
    }
    # chain_rows_of <entries> <id>: the workbook's calcChain rows, those
    # identical and unflagged, and those dropped (change NSI).
    chain_rows_of() {
      awk -F'\t' -v id="$2" '
        NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) col[$i] = i; next }
        $col["id"] == id && $col["name"] == "xl/calcChain.xml" { n++; if ($col["status"] == "identical" && $col["flags"] == "") s++; if ($col["status"] == "dropped") d++ }
        END { print n + 0, s + 0, d + 0 }' "$1"
    }
    # The rule's controls: accepted where it holds, refused on each planted row
    # where it does not (change NWW).
    etsv() { { printf 'id\tname\tstatus\tflags\n'; printf "$@"; } >"$B/ce.tsv"; }
    KEPT='w\txl/styles.xml\tidentical\t\nw\txl/worksheets/sheet1.xml\tidentical\t\n'
    TOUCHED='w\t[Content_Types].xml\tchanged\tdescriptor\nw\txl/workbook.xml\tchanged\tdescriptor\nw\txl/_rels/workbook.xml.rels\tchanged\t\n'
    ADDED='w\txl/chartsheets/sheet1.xml\tadded\t\nw\txl/chartsheets/_rels/sheet1.xml.rels\tadded\t\nw\txl/drawings/drawing3.xml\tadded\t\nw\txl/drawings/_rels/drawing3.xml.rels\tadded\t\nw\txl/charts/chart7.xml\tadded\t\n'
    cn() { chartsheet_named "$B/ce.tsv" w; }
    etsv "$KEPT$TOUCHED$ADDED"
    check "control: chartsheet_named accepts a planted workbook's rows" "$(yn cn)"
    check "control: added_chartsheet reads the planted chartsheet's name" "$(yn [ "$(added_chartsheet "$B/ce.tsv" w)" = xl/chartsheets/sheet1.xml ])"
    etsv "$KEPT${TOUCHED}w\txl/chartsheets/sheet1.xml\tadded\t\nw\txl/chartsheets/_rels/sheet1.xml.rels\tadded\t\nw\txl/drawings/drawing3.xml\tadded\t\nw\txl/drawings/_rels/drawing3.xml.rels\tadded\t\n"
    check "control: chartsheet_named refuses no chart part added" "$(ynnot cn)"
    etsv "$KEPT$TOUCHED${ADDED}w\txl/charts/chart8.xml\tadded\t\n"
    check "control: chartsheet_named refuses two chart parts added" "$(ynnot cn)"
    etsv "$KEPT${TOUCHED}w\txl/chartsheets/sheet1.xml\tadded\t\nw\txl/chartsheets/_rels/sheet2.xml.rels\tadded\t\nw\txl/drawings/drawing3.xml\tadded\t\nw\txl/drawings/_rels/drawing3.xml.rels\tadded\t\nw\txl/charts/chart7.xml\tadded\t\n"
    check "control: chartsheet_named refuses a chartsheet rels part of another chartsheet" "$(ynnot cn)"
    etsv "$KEPT${TOUCHED}w\txl/chartsheets/sheet1.xml\tadded\t\nw\txl/chartsheets/_rels/sheet1.xml.rels\tadded\t\nw\txl/drawings/drawing3.xml\tadded\t\nw\txl/drawings/_rels/drawing4.xml.rels\tadded\t\nw\txl/charts/chart7.xml\tadded\t\n"
    check "control: chartsheet_named refuses a drawing rels part of another drawing" "$(ynnot cn)"
    etsv "${KEPT}w\t[Content_Types].xml\tchanged\tdescriptor\nw\txl/workbook.xml\tchanged\tdescriptor\nw\txl/_rels/other.xml.rels\tchanged\t\n$ADDED"
    check "control: chartsheet_named refuses a changed rels part not the workbook part's" "$(ynnot cn)"
    etsv "${KEPT}w\t[Content_Types].xml\tchanged\tdescriptor\nw\txl/workbook.xml\tchanged\tdescriptor\n$ADDED"
    check "control: chartsheet_named refuses the workbook's rels part unchanged" "$(ynnot cn)"
    etsv "$KEPT${TOUCHED}w\tother/chartsheets/sheet1.xml\tadded\t\nw\tother/chartsheets/_rels/sheet1.xml.rels\tadded\t\nw\txl/drawings/drawing3.xml\tadded\t\nw\txl/drawings/_rels/drawing3.xml.rels\tadded\t\nw\txl/charts/chart7.xml\tadded\t\n"
    check "control: chartsheet_named refuses a chartsheet not beside the workbook part" "$(ynnot cn)"
    etsv "${KEPT}w\txl/theme/theme1.xml\tchanged\t\n$TOUCHED$ADDED"
    check "control: chartsheet_named refuses another part changed" "$(ynnot cn)"
    etsv "${KEPT}w\txl/styles.xml\tidentical\tmtime\n$TOUCHED$ADDED"
    check "control: chartsheet_named refuses an identical row flagged" "$(ynnot cn)"
    etsv "$KEPT${TOUCHED}w\txl/chartsheets/sheet1.xml\tadded\t\nw\txl/chartsheets/_rels/sheet1.xml.rels\tadded\t\nw\txl/drawings/drawing3.xml\tadded\t\nw\txl/drawings/_rels/drawing3.xml.rels\tadded\t\nw\txl/charts/chart7.xml\tadded\tdescriptor\n"
    check "control: chartsheet_named refuses an added row flagged" "$(ynnot cn)"
    etsv "$KEPT$TOUCHED${ADDED}w\txl/calcChain.xml\tdropped\t\n"
    check "control: chartsheet_named refuses a dropped row" "$(ynnot cn)"
    etsv "$KEPT$TOUCHED${ADDED}w\txl/calcChain.xml\trecompressed\t\n"
    check "control: chartsheet_named refuses a recompressed row" "$(ynnot cn)"
    etsv "$KEPT$TOUCHED${ADDED}w\txl/media/image1.png\tadded\t\n"
    check "control: chartsheet_named refuses another part added" "$(ynnot cn)"
    cn_none() { chartsheet_named "$B/ce.tsv" v; }
    etsv "$KEPT$TOUCHED$ADDED"
    check "control: chartsheet_named refuses a workbook with no rows" "$(ynnot cn_none)"
    check "control: added_chartsheet reads nothing for a workbook with no rows" "$(yn [ -z "$(added_chartsheet "$B/ce.tsv" v)" ])"
    etsv 'w\txl/styles.xml\tidentical\t\nw\txl/calcChain.xml\tidentical\t\n'
    check "control: chain_rows_of reads the planted workbook's one calcChain row, identical and unflagged" "$(yn [ "$(chain_rows_of "$B/ce.tsv" w)" = "1 1 0" ])"
    etsv 'w\txl/styles.xml\tidentical\t\nw\txl/calcChain.xml\tdropped\t\n'
    check "control: chain_rows_of reads a dropped calcChain row as dropped" "$(yn [ "$(chain_rows_of "$B/ce.tsv" w)" = "1 0 1" ])"
    # The input's sheet count: the <sheet> children of <sheets> in the part the
    # package relationship of type officeDocument names, either form, read with
    # zipfile and ElementTree; one number printed per workbook (change NWW).
    cat >"$B/sheetcount.py" <<'PY'
    """Prints the sheet count of each workbook given: the <sheet> children of the
    <sheets> element of the workbook part, the part _rels/.rels names with an
    officeDocument relationship of either namespace form; "error" for a
    workbook this cannot read. Counts only: no name, part or path printed."""
    import posixpath
    import sys
    import zipfile
    import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
    
    sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
    
    
    def local(tag):
        return tag.rsplit("}", 1)[-1]
    
    
    for path in sys.argv[1:]:
        try:
            z = zipfile.ZipFile(path)
            rels = ET.fromstring(z.read("_rels/.rels"))
            targets = [r.get("Target") for r in rels if local(r.tag) == "Relationship"
                       and (r.get("Type") or "").endswith("/officeDocument")]
            part = posixpath.normpath(targets[0].lstrip("/"))
            root = ET.fromstring(z.read(part))
            sheets = [c for c in root if local(c.tag) == "sheets"]
            print(sum(1 for s in sheets for c in s if local(c.tag) == "sheet"))
        except Exception:
            print("error")
    PY
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/sheetcount.py"
    # refusal_of <run dir> <id> <label>: the layer's one "error: " line when the
    # row is a refusal, else nothing.
    refusal_of() { sed -n '1s/^error: //p' "$1/$2/stderr.$3.txt"; }
    
    
    echo
    echo "## TMPDIR for the corpus runs, on the disk"
    RUNTMP=$B/tmp-run
    mkdir "$RUNTMP" || exit 2
    dev_tmp=$(stat -c %d "$RUNTMP")
    dev_corpus=$(stat -c %d "$CORPUS/corpus")
    dev_proc=$(stat -c %d /proc)
    echo "command: mkdir <work>/tmp-run; stat -c %d <work>/tmp-run <corpus>/corpus /proc; df --output=fstype,target <work>/tmp-run <corpus>/corpus"
    echo "  device of TMPDIR (<work>/tmp-run): $dev_tmp; of the corpus directory (<corpus>/corpus): $dev_corpus; of /proc (the control): $dev_proc"
    df --output=fstype,target "$RUNTMP" "$CORPUS/corpus" | sed 's/^/    /'
    check "TMPDIR for the corpus runs and the corpus directory are on one device" "$(yn [ "$dev_tmp" = "$dev_corpus" ])"
    check "control: the same comparison tells /proc's device from the corpus directory's" "$(yn [ "$dev_proc" != "$dev_corpus" ])"
    
    cat >"$B/reccheck.py" <<'PY'
    """This log's check of a passthrough record against its run directory, for
    every label the directory holds. Reads the record's .txt and .md and the run
    directory's summary.<label>.tsv, entries.<label>.tsv and each workbook's
    diff.<label>.tsv; prints one "name: yes|no" line per check and one line of
    counts. It imports only the part-family rules from
    scripts/passthrough-record.py, so the check covers the record's tables and
    its counting, not the family names. Change VJ: the dropped families are an
    input, as the changed and added ones are."""
    import importlib.util
    import os
    import sys
    
    sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
    rec_script, run_dir, txt, md, want_changed, want_added, want_dropped, tool_arg = sys.argv[1:9]
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("record", rec_script)
    record = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    spec.loader.exec_module(record)
    
    
    def lines(path):
        out = open(path, encoding="utf-8").read().split("\n")
        return out[:-1] if out and out[-1] == "" else out
    
    
    def listed(value):
        return value.split(",") if value else []
    
    
    labels = [l for l in ("host", "i686") if os.path.exists("%s/summary.%s.tsv" % (run_dir, l))]
    tables = "\n".join(lines(txt)).split("\n\n")
    summary, entries, xml = [], [], ["\t".join(record.XML_HEADER)]
    per_label = {}
    for label in labels:
        s = lines("%s/summary.%s.tsv" % (run_dir, label))
        e = lines("%s/entries.%s.tsv" % (run_dir, label))
        summary = summary or [s[0]]
        entries = entries or [e[0]]
        summary += s[1:]
        entries += e[1:]
        x = []
        for row in s[1:]:
            cells = dict(zip(s[0].split("\t"), row.split("\t")))
            if cells["outcome"] != "ok" or cells["diff_exit"] not in ("0", "1"):
                continue
            for line in lines("%s/%s/diff.%s.tsv" % (run_dir, cells["id"], label)):
                c = line.split("\t")
                if c[0] == "xml":
                    x.append("\t".join([cells["id"], label] + c + [""] * (10 - 2 - len(c))))
        xml += x
        per_label[label] = (e, x)
    checks = [
        ("three tables", len(tables) == 3),
        ("the summary table is every label's summary", len(tables) == 3 and tables[0].split("\n") == summary),
        ("the entries table is every label's entries", len(tables) == 3 and tables[1].split("\n") == entries),
        ("the xml table is every compared workbook's xml rows", len(tables) == 3 and tables[2].split("\n") == xml),
    ]
    text = lines(md)
    
    
    def section(title):
        out, on = [], False
        for line in text:
            if line == "## " + title:
                on = True
                continue
            if on and line.startswith("## "):
                break
            if on and line.startswith("| ") and not line.startswith("| ---"):
                out.append(line)
        return out[1:]
    
    
    def row(cells):
        return "| " + " | ".join(str(c) for c in cells) + " |"
    
    
    cols = ("entries",) + record.STATUSES + ("flagged",) + record.FLAGS
    xcols = ("compared", "parse_errors", "names_equal", "values_equal", "in_only", "out_only")
    for label in labels:
        e, x = per_label[label]
        head = e[0].split("\t")
        fam = {}
        for line in e[1:]:
            r = dict(zip(head, line.split("\t")))
            c = fam.setdefault(record.family(r["name"]), dict.fromkeys(cols, 0))
            c["entries"] += 1
            c[r["status"]] = c.get(r["status"], 0) + 1
            flags = [f for f in r["flags"].split(",") if f]
            c["flagged"] += 1 if flags else 0
            for f in flags:
                c[f] = c.get(f, 0) + 1
        want = [row([f] + [fam[f][k] for k in cols]) for f in record.FAMILIES if f in fam]
        want.append(row(["total"] + [sum(fam[f][k] for f in fam) for k in cols]))
        checks.append(("%s: each family row of Entries by part family" % label, section("Entries by part family: " + label) == want))
        xf, cur = {}, None
        for line in x:
            c = line.split("\t")
            name, kind = c[3], c[4]
            if kind == "parse":
                cur = xf.setdefault(record.family(name), dict.fromkeys(xcols, 0))
                cur["compared"] += 1
                parsed = c[5] == "ok" and c[6] == "ok"
                cur["parse_errors"] += 0 if parsed else 1
                differ = False
            elif kind in ("element", "attribute"):
                differ = True
            elif kind == "values":
                cur["names_equal"] += 1 if parsed and not differ else 0
                cur["values_equal"] += 1 if c[7] == "0" and c[8] == "0" else 0
                cur["in_only"] += int(c[7])
                cur["out_only"] += int(c[8])
        want = [row([f] + [xf[f][k] for k in xcols]) for f in record.FAMILIES if f in xf]
        want.append(row(["total"] + [sum(xf[f][k] for f in xf) for k in xcols]))
        checks.append(("%s: each family row of the XML comparison" % label, section("XML comparison of changed entries: " + label) == want))
        changed_f = sorted(f for f in fam if fam[f].get("changed"))
        dropped_f = sorted(f for f in fam if fam[f].get("dropped"))
        added_f = sorted(f for f in fam if fam[f].get("added"))
        checks.append(("%s: the xml families are the changed entries' families" % label, sorted(xf) == changed_f))
        checks.append(("%s: the changed entries' families are %s" % (label, want_changed or "none"), changed_f == listed(want_changed)))
        checks.append(("%s: the dropped entries' families are %s" % (label, want_dropped or "none"), dropped_f == listed(want_dropped)))
        checks.append(("%s: the added entries' families are %s" % (label, want_added or "none"), added_f == listed(want_added)))
    checks.append(("the record's Targets line", "- Targets: " + ", ".join(labels) in text))
    checks.append(("the record's Tool arguments line", "- Tool arguments: " + tool_arg in text))
    for name, ok in checks:
        print("%s: %s" % (name, "yes" if ok else "no"))
    print("labels %s; summary rows %d; entry rows %d; xml rows %d" % (",".join(labels), len(summary) - 1, len(entries) - 1, len(xml) - 1))
    PY
    fams_of() {
      python3 -I -B -c 'import importlib.util, sys
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("record", sys.argv[1])
    record = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    spec.loader.exec_module(record)
    rows = [l.split("\t", 1) for l in open(sys.argv[2]).read().split("\n") if l]
    print(",".join(sorted({record.family(n) for (k, n) in rows if k == sys.argv[3]})))' scripts/passthrough-record.py "$1" "$2"
    }
    inst_same() { cmp -s "$RECORDS/$1" "$RECORDS_DEST/$1" && [ "$(stat -c %a "$RECORDS_DEST/$1")" = 644 ]; }
    # Change JI: no bytecode was written, so there is nothing to remove.
    no_pycache() { [ ! -e scripts/__pycache__ ]; }
    # Change NVX: the per-sample block P2 ran once, run for each sample in
    # turn, here the one (change NWY): line_ok and named give the sample's
    # rule (change NWW); every file under <work> carries the sample's word.
    # line_ok <tool line> <id>: the line by the rule, with the input's sheet
    # count, read from the corpus input, and the added chartsheet's name's
    # length, read from the rows.
    line_ok() {
      case $SAMPLE in
        chartsheet) chartsheet_line_ok "$1" "$(PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -I -B "$B/sheetcount.py" "$CORPUS/corpus/$2.$ext")" "$(added_chartsheet "$ENT" "$2" | awk '{ print length($0) }')" 0 ;;
        *) return 1 ;;
      esac
    }
    # form_of: the chartsheet sample has one form (change NWY).
    form_of() { echo 0; }
    # named <entries> <id>: the workbook's rows by the sample's rule.
    named() {
      case $SAMPLE in
        chartsheet) chartsheet_named "$1" "$2" ;;
        *) return 1 ;;
      esac
    }
    for SAMPLE in $SAMPLES; do
    EDIT=${EDITS[$SAMPLE]}
    STEM=${STEMS[$SAMPLE]}
    O=$RUN_OUT_ROOT/$RUN-$SAMPLE
    case $SAMPLE in
      chartsheet)
        LINE_WHAT="one chart of two series, the sheet list one longer than the input's, the part name's length the added chartsheet entry's, no kept chartsheet chart"
        ROWS_WHAT="nothing dropped or recompressed, files_identical no in every ok row; each workbook's rows by the chartsheet rule above"
        SUMMARY_WHAT="nothing dropped or recompressed"
        FORM_WHAT="one form, a chartsheet added"
        ;;
    esac
    for label in host i686; do
      var=PT_$label; PT=${!var}; var=XD_$label; XD=${!var}
      echo
      echo "## $SAMPLE: $label run, --tool-arg $EDIT"
      echo "command: TMPDIR=<work>/tmp-run scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label $label --passthrough <work>/bin/$label/emend-copy --xlsx-diff <work>/bin/$label/xlsx-diff --out <runs>/$RUN-$SAMPLE --libreoffice $IMAGE --lo-timeout $LO_TIMEOUT_S --timeout 300 --tool-arg $EDIT"
      started=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
      TMPDIR=$RUNTMP scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label "$label" --passthrough "$PT" --xlsx-diff "$XD" --out "$O" \
        --libreoffice "$IMAGE" --lo-timeout "$LO_TIMEOUT_S" --timeout 300 --tool-arg "$EDIT" \
        >"$B/run-$SAMPLE-$label.stdout" 2>"$B/run-$SAMPLE-$label.stderr" </dev/null
      rc=$?
      echo "  started $started; ended $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ); exit $rc; stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$B/run-$SAMPLE-$label.stderr")"
      sed 's/^/    /' "$B/run-$SAMPLE-$label.stdout"
      check "$SAMPLE $label: the run exits 0" "$(yn [ "$rc" = 0 ])"
      check "$SAMPLE $label: its stderr is empty" "$(yn [ ! -s "$B/run-$SAMPLE-$label.stderr" ])"
      n_left=$(find "$RUNTMP" -mindepth 1 | wc -l)
      echo "  entries left in <work>/tmp-run after the run: $n_left"
      check "$SAMPLE $label: the runs' TMPDIR is empty after the run" "$(yn [ "$n_left" = 0 ])"
      SUM=$O/summary.$label.tsv
      ENT=$O/entries.$label.tsv
      rows=$(awk 'NR > 1' "$SUM" | wc -l)
      n_ok=$(count_where "$SUM" outcome ok)
      # The refusals, by id and message.
      : >"$B/refused-$SAMPLE-$label"
      while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
        if [ "$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$id" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next } $k["id"] == id { print $k["outcome"] " " $k["exit"] }' "$SUM")" = "error 2" ] \
           && [ "$(count_lines "$O/$id/stderr.$label.txt")" = 1 ] && [ -n "$(refusal_of "$O" "$id" "$label")" ]; then
          printf '%s\t%s\n' "$id" "$(refusal_of "$O" "$id" "$label")" >>"$B/refused-$SAMPLE-$label"
        fi
      done <"$B/order"
      n_ref=$(count_lines "$B/refused-$SAMPLE-$label")
      echo "  summary rows: $rows; outcome ok: $n_ok; refused by the layer (a finding; fails the summary): $n_ref"
      sed 's/^/    refused: /' "$B/refused-$SAMPLE-$label"
      echo "  among the ok rows: lo ok $(count_ok_where "$SUM" lo ok); lo_in ok $(count_ok_where "$SUM" lo_in ok); leftover no $(count_ok_where "$SUM" leftover no); order_preserved yes $(count_ok_where "$SUM" order_preserved yes); comment_equal yes $(count_ok_where "$SUM" comment_equal yes); files_identical no $(count_ok_where "$SUM" files_identical no), yes $(count_ok_where "$SUM" files_identical yes)"
      echo "  every row: lo_in ok $(count_where "$SUM" lo_in ok); leftover no $(count_where "$SUM" leftover no)"
      echo "  entry totals: identical $(sum_col "$SUM" identical), recompressed $(sum_col "$SUM" recompressed), changed $(sum_col "$SUM" changed), dropped $(sum_col "$SUM" dropped), added $(sum_col "$SUM" added), flagged $(sum_col "$SUM" flagged)"
      echo "  the entries table's rows by status: identical $(status_rows "$ENT" identical), recompressed $(status_rows "$ENT" recompressed), changed $(status_rows "$ENT" changed), dropped $(status_rows "$ENT" dropped), added $(status_rows "$ENT" added)"
      echo "  the entry totals the ok rows imply (an edit sample; changes NVW and NVX): $ROWS_WHAT"
      summary_ok() {
        local col st
        [ "$rows" = "$manifest_rows" ] || return 1
        [ "$n_ok" = "$rows" ] && [ "$n_ref" = 0 ] || return 1
        for col in "lo ok" "lo_in ok" "leftover no" "order_preserved yes" "comment_equal yes" "files_identical no"; do
          [ "$(count_ok_where "$SUM" ${col% *} ${col#* })" = "$n_ok" ] || return 1
        done
        [ "$(count_where "$SUM" lo_in ok)" = "$rows" ] || return 1
        [ "$(count_where "$SUM" leftover no)" = "$rows" ] || return 1
        if [ "$SAMPLE" = chartsheet ]; then
          for st in dropped recompressed; do
            [ "$(sum_col "$SUM" "$st")" = 0 ] || return 1
          done
        fi
        for st in identical recompressed changed dropped added; do
          [ "$(sum_col "$SUM" "$st")" = "$(status_rows "$ENT" "$st")" ] || return 1
        done
      }
      check "$SAMPLE $label: every row ok; every row's input opens (lo_in ok) with no leftover; every output opens (lo ok), order and comment kept, files_identical no; $SUMMARY_WHAT; the summary's status totals the entries table's (change NVX)" "$(yn summary_ok)"
      echo "  per ok workbook: id and the tool's line (counts and flags only)"
      : >"$B/lines-$SAMPLE-$label"
      : >"$B/made-$SAMPLE-$label"
      nwb=0; nline=0; nentries=0; nform=0
      nchain=0; nchain_same=0; nchain_drop=0
      while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
        if [ -n "$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$id" '$1 == id' "$B/refused-$SAMPLE-$label")" ]; then continue; fi
        nwb=$((nwb + 1))
        e=$(cat "$O/$id/stdout.$label.txt")
        printf '%s\t%s\n' "$id" "$e" >>"$B/lines-$SAMPLE-$label"
        printf '    %s %s\n' "$id" "$(printf '%s' "$e" | tr '\t' ' ')"
        form=$(form_of "$ENT" "$id" "$e")
        printf '%s\t%s\n' "$id" "$form" >>"$B/made-$SAMPLE-$label"
        if [ "$form" = 1 ]; then nform=$((nform + 1)); fi
        if LC_ALL=C "$G" -qxF "$id" "$B/chain-ids"; then
          cr=$(chain_rows_of "$ENT" "$id")
          set -- $cr
          nchain=$((nchain + $1)); nchain_same=$((nchain_same + $2)); nchain_drop=$((nchain_drop + $3))
        fi
        if line_ok "$e" "$id"; then nline=$((nline + 1)); else echo "    $id: the tool's line is not what the spec reads"; fi
        if named "$ENT" "$id" "$form" "$e"; then nentries=$((nentries + 1)); else echo "    $id: the entry rows are not what the rule gives for the form read, $form"; fi
      done <"$B/order"
      echo "  ok workbooks read: $nwb; the line as the spec reads: $nline; entry rows as the rule gives: $nentries; $FORM_WHAT: $nform, not: $((nwb - nform))"
      check "$SAMPLE $label: every ok workbook's line was read" "$(yn [ "$nwb" = "$n_ok" ])"
      check "$SAMPLE $label: every line is what the spec reads ($LINE_WHAT; change NWW)" "$(yn [ "$nline" = "$n_ok" ])"
      check "$SAMPLE $label: every ok workbook's entry rows are as the rule gives (change NWW)" "$(yn [ "$nentries" = "$n_ok" ])"
      echo "  calcChain rows in the ok rows of the chain workbooks: $nchain; identical and unflagged: $nchain_same; dropped: $nchain_drop (change NSI)"
      chain_kept() { [ "$nchain" = "$N_CHAIN" ] && [ "$nchain_same" = "$nchain" ] && [ "$nchain_drop" = 0 ]; }
      check "$SAMPLE $label: every chain workbook has one calcChain row, identical and unflagged, none dropped (change NSI)" "$(yn chain_kept)"
      R=$O/run.$label.tsv
      args=$(row_field "$R" tool_args)
      bins_in_row() { [ "$(awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next } NR == 2 { print $k["passthrough_sha256"] " " $k["xlsx_diff_sha256"] " " $k["commit"] }' "$R")" = "$(sha_of "$PT") $(sha_of "$XD") $C" ]; }
      check "$SAMPLE $label: the run row records the size log's two release binaries, the copies in <work>/bin, by sha256 and the phase commit (change NXH)" "$(yn bins_in_row)"
      check "$SAMPLE $label: the run row's tool_args is $EDIT" "$(yn [ "$args" = "$EDIT" ])"
    done
    check "$SAMPLE: the same workbooks are refused on both targets, with the same messages (none)" "$(yn cmp -s "$B/refused-$SAMPLE-host" "$B/refused-$SAMPLE-i686")"
    cp "$B/refused-$SAMPLE-host" "$B/c-refused"; printf 'x\tsome message\n' >>"$B/c-refused"
    check "control: the same comparison tells a planted refusal list from the host's" "$(ynnot cmp -s "$B/c-refused" "$B/refused-$SAMPLE-i686")"
    mkdir -p "$B/c-refrun/r1"
    printf 'error: a planted message\n' >"$B/c-refrun/r1/stderr.host.txt"
    ref_read() { [ "$(refusal_of "$B/c-refrun" r1 host)" = "a planted message" ]; }
    check "control: refusal_of reads a planted refusal's message" "$(yn ref_read)"
    : >"$B/c-refrun/r1/stderr.host.txt"
    ref_none() { [ -z "$(refusal_of "$B/c-refrun" r1 host)" ]; }
    check "control: refusal_of reads nothing from an empty standard error" "$(yn ref_none)"
    first_line() { awk -F'\t' -v id="$1" '$1 == id { sub(/^[^\t]*\t/, ""); print; exit }' "$B/lines-$SAMPLE-host"; }
    entries_ctl() {
      local id
      id=$(head -n 1 "$B/order" | cut -f1)
      named "$O/entries.host.tsv" "${id}x" 0 "$(first_line "$id")"
    }
    check "control: $SAMPLE: named refuses the first workbook's id with a letter appended, which has no rows" "$(ynnot entries_ctl)"
    first_line_ctl() { local id ext ENT; id=$(head -n 1 "$B/order" | cut -f1); ext=$(head -n 1 "$B/order" | cut -f2); ENT=$O/entries.host.tsv; line_ok "$(first_line "$id" | sed 's/series=2/series=3/')" "$id"; }
    check "control: $SAMPLE: line_ok refuses the first workbook's host line with series 3 (change NWY)" "$(ynnot first_line_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "### $SAMPLE: the corpus totals over the host's ok workbooks (counts only; change NVX)"
    total_of() { cut -f2- "$1" | tr '\t ' '\n\n' | sed -n "s/^$2=//p" | awk '{ n += $1 } END { print n + 0 }'; }
    wbs_of() { cut -f2- "$1" | tr '\t ' '\n\n' | sed -n "s/^$2=//p" | awk '$1 > 0 { n++ } END { print n + 0 }'; }
    keys_var=KEYS_$SAMPLE
    for k in ${!keys_var}; do
      echo "    $k: $(total_of "$B/lines-$SAMPLE-host" "$k") in $(wbs_of "$B/lines-$SAMPLE-host" "$k") workbooks"
    done
    read_all() { [ "$(total_of "$B/lines-$SAMPLE-host" charts)" = "$manifest_rows" ] && [ "$(total_of "$B/lines-$SAMPLE-host" series)" = "$((2 * manifest_rows))" ] && [ "$(total_of "$B/lines-$SAMPLE-host" kept_charts)" = 0 ] && [ "$(count_lines "$B/lines-$SAMPLE-host")" = "$manifest_rows" ]; }
    check "every workbook's chartsheet read back with one chart of two series, charts $(total_of "$B/lines-$SAMPLE-host" charts) and series $(total_of "$B/lines-$SAMPLE-host" series) of $manifest_rows and $((2 * manifest_rows)), and no kept chartsheet chart (change NWY)" "$(yn read_all)"
    
    echo
    echo "### $SAMPLE: the two labels' outputs"
    same_out=0
    nboth=0
    while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
      if [ -n "$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$id" '$1 == id' "$B/refused-$SAMPLE-host")" ]; then continue; fi
      nboth=$((nboth + 1))
      if cmp -s "$O/$id/out.host.$ext" "$O/$id/out.i686.$ext"; then same_out=$((same_out + 1)); else echo "    $id: the outputs differ"; fi
    done <"$B/order"
    echo "  ok workbooks: $nboth; whose host and i686 outputs are byte for byte the same: $same_out"
    check "$SAMPLE: every output is the same on both targets" "$(yn [ "$same_out" = "$nboth" ])"
    check "$SAMPLE: both targets printed the same line for every ok workbook" "$(yn cmp -s "$B/lines-$SAMPLE-host" "$B/lines-$SAMPLE-i686")"
    cp "$B/lines-$SAMPLE-host" "$B/c-lines"; printf 'x\n' >>"$B/c-lines"
    check "control: the same comparison tells a line list with one line added" "$(ynnot cmp -s "$B/c-lines" "$B/lines-$SAMPLE-i686")"
    
    echo
    echo "## the $SAMPLE run's record pair"
    echo "command: python3 -I -B scripts/passthrough-record.py --run <runs>/$RUN-$SAMPLE --out <scripts>/out/records --stem $STEM (changes NTJ, NUW and NVX)"
    python3 -I -B scripts/passthrough-record.py --run "$O" --out "$RECORDS" --stem "$STEM" >"$B/record-$SAMPLE.out" 2>&1
    rrc=$?
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/record-$SAMPLE.out"
    check "$SAMPLE: the record script exits 0" "$(yn [ "$rrc" = 0 ])"
    RTXT=$RECORDS/$STEM.txt
    RMD=$RECORDS/$STEM.md
    # The families: the names of the host entries table's changed, added and
    # dropped rows (change NSR), against the sample's (changes NUW and NVX).
    awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next } $k["status"] ~ /^(changed|added|dropped)$/ { print $k["status"] "\t" $k["name"] }' "$O/entries.host.tsv" >"$B/w-$SAMPLE.parts"
    check "$SAMPLE: some changed, added or dropped name in the host entries table ($(count_lines "$B/w-$SAMPLE.parts") names; change NSR)" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/w-$SAMPLE.parts")" -ge 1 ])"
    FAM_CHANGED=$(fams_of "$B/w-$SAMPLE.parts" changed)
    FAM_ADDED=$(fams_of "$B/w-$SAMPLE.parts" added)
    FAM_DROPPED=$(fams_of "$B/w-$SAMPLE.parts" dropped)
    echo "  the families: changed ${FAM_CHANGED:-none}; added ${FAM_ADDED:-none}; dropped ${FAM_DROPPED:-none}"
    case $SAMPLE in
      chartsheet) WANT_FAMS="content-types,rels,workbook chart,drawing,rels,worksheet -" ;;
    esac
    fams_ok() { [ "$FAM_CHANGED ${FAM_ADDED:--} ${FAM_DROPPED:--}" = "$WANT_FAMS" ]; }
    check "$SAMPLE: the changed, added and dropped families are the sample's: $WANT_FAMS (- for none; changes NUW and NWW)" "$(yn fams_ok)"
    fams_ctl() { local FAM_ADDED=planted; fams_ok; }
    check "control: the same check refuses a planted added family" "$(ynnot fams_ctl)"
    python3 -I -B "$B/reccheck.py" scripts/passthrough-record.py "$O" "$RTXT" "$RMD" "$FAM_CHANGED" "$FAM_ADDED" "$FAM_DROPPED" "$EDIT" >"$B/reccheck-$SAMPLE.out" 2>&1
    echo "  exit: $?"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/reccheck-$SAMPLE.out"
    rec_all() { [ "$(count_matches -E ': yes$' "$B/reccheck-$SAMPLE.out")" = 18 ] && [ "$(count_matches -E ': no$' "$B/reccheck-$SAMPLE.out")" = 0 ]; }
    check "$SAMPLE: the record's three tables are the run directory's, and its family tables are counted from them (eighteen checks: four, six per label, two)" "$(yn rec_all)"
    awk '!done && /^[|] total [|]/ { done = 1; next } { print }' "$RMD" >"$B/c-rec.md"
    python3 -I -B "$B/reccheck.py" scripts/passthrough-record.py "$O" "$RTXT" "$B/c-rec.md" "$FAM_CHANGED" "$FAM_ADDED" "$FAM_DROPPED" "$EDIT" >"$B/c-reccheck.out" 2>&1
    sed '2d' "$RTXT" >"$B/c-rec.txt"
    python3 -I -B "$B/reccheck.py" scripts/passthrough-record.py "$O" "$B/c-rec.txt" "$RMD" "$FAM_CHANGED" "$FAM_ADDED" "$FAM_DROPPED" "$EDIT" >"$B/c-reccheck2.out" 2>&1
    python3 -I -B "$B/reccheck.py" scripts/passthrough-record.py "$O" "$RTXT" "$RMD" "$FAM_CHANGED" "$FAM_ADDED" "planted" "$EDIT" >"$B/c-reccheck3.out" 2>&1
    rec_ctl() { [ "$(count_matches -E ': no$' "$B/c-reccheck.out")" -ge 1 ] && [ "$(count_matches -F "the summary table is every label's summary: no" "$B/c-reccheck2.out")" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same check finds an .md with a family table's total row dropped and a .txt one summary row short" "$(yn rec_ctl)"
    rec_drop() { [ "$(count_matches -E "the dropped entries' families are planted: no\$" "$B/c-reccheck3.out")" = 2 ]; }
    check "control: the same check finds the dropped families differ from a planted family, on each label" "$(yn rec_drop)"
    check "the record script and the record check left no scripts/__pycache__ (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE)" "$(yn no_pycache)"
    echo "command: install -m 644 <scripts>/out/records/$STEM.md <scripts>/out/records/$STEM.txt <repo>/$RECORDS_DEST/"
    install -m 644 "$RMD" "$RTXT" "$RECORDS_DEST"/ && INSTALLED+=("$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM.md" "$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM.txt")
    echo "  exit: $?"
    for f in "$STEM.md" "$STEM.txt"; do
      echo "    installed $RECORDS_DEST/$f: sha256 $(sha_of "$RECORDS_DEST/$f"), $(wc -c <"$RECORDS_DEST/$f") bytes, mode $(stat -c %a "$RECORDS_DEST/$f")"
      check "the installed $f is the written one, mode 644" "$(yn inst_same "$f")"
    done
    done
    echo
    echo "## the corpus run against P2's, the run the record P2's record commit added names, by sha256 (specs/0038 \"P3\" and ruling M: the P2 runs rerun with the size log's release binaries, byte-identical by sha256; P2's change NXB's form; a difference is a finding, not a fix; change NXI)"
    # run_of_md <record .md>: the run directory the committed record names.
    run_of_md() { git show "$C:$1" 2>/dev/null | sed -n 's/^Written by .* from the run directory `\([^`]*\)`.*$/\1/p' | head -n 1; }
    P2_PAT=records/m6p1-p2-
    P2_WANT=records/m6p1-p2-2026-10-19-2a706dc.txt
    P2_MD=$(git show --name-only --format= "$REC" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -E "^${P2_PAT}[0-9-]+-[0-9a-f]{7}[.]md\$")
    P2_TXT=$(git show --name-only --format= "$REC" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -E "^${P2_PAT}[0-9-]+-[0-9a-f]{7}[.]txt\$")
    echo "command: git show --name-only --format= <P2's record commit>, the chartsheet record's .md and .txt it added: ${P2_MD:-none} ${P2_TXT:-none}"
    check "P2's record commit added exactly one chartsheet record .md and one .txt (change NXI)" "$(yn [ "$(printf '%s\n%s\n' "$P2_MD" "$P2_TXT" | count_matches -E '^records/' /dev/stdin)" = 2 ])"
    check "the record is the one this phase names, $P2_WANT (change NXI)" "$(yn [ "$P2_TXT" = "$P2_WANT" ])"
    p2_later() { [ -z "$(git log --format=%H "$REC..$C" -- "${P2_PAT}*.md")" ]; }
    check "no later commit adds a record of that stem, so it is the latest committed (change NXI)" "$(yn p2_later)"
    p2_want_ctl() { [ "$P2_TXT" = records/m6p1-open-2026-10-19-2a706dc.txt ]; }
    check "control: the record-name check refuses the record against P2's open-check record's name" "$(ynnot p2_want_ctl)"
    P2_RUN_NAME=$(run_of_md "$P2_MD")
    P2_RUN=$CORPUS/runs/$P2_RUN_NAME
    echo "  the run directory the record names: <corpus>/runs/${P2_RUN_NAME:-none} (read only)"
    p2_run_ok() { [ -n "$P2_RUN_NAME" ] && [ -d "$P2_RUN" ] && [ -f "$P2_RUN/summary.host.tsv" ] && [ -f "$P2_RUN/summary.i686.tsv" ]; }
    check "the run directory is there with both labels' summaries (change NXI)" "$(yn p2_run_ok)"
    p2_run_ctl() { local P2_RUN=$CORPUS/runs/no-such-run; p2_run_ok; }
    check "control: the same check refuses a run directory that is not there" "$(ynnot p2_run_ctl)"
    check "the run's run row names --chartsheet-sample (change NXI)" "$(yn [ "$(row_field "$P2_RUN/run.host.tsv" tool_args)" = --chartsheet-sample ])"
    check "the run's run row names P2's record commit's parent, P2's phase commit (change NXI)" "$(yn [ "$(row_field "$P2_RUN/run.host.tsv" commit)" = "$(git rev-parse "$REC~1")" ])"
    check "control: the run row check refuses the run's row against this phase's commit" "$(ynnot [ "$(row_field "$P2_RUN/run.host.tsv" commit)" = "$C" ])"
    # same_row <run dir> <earlier run dir> <id> <ext> <label>: the row's output
    # and its tool line in the two run directories, both there, the same by
    # sha256 (M5 part 5 P4's change NWB, its P2's change NVS's form).
    same_row() {
      local f
      for f in "out.$5.$4" "stdout.$5.txt"; do
        [ -f "$1/$3/$f" ] && [ -f "$2/$3/$f" ] || return 1
        [ "$(sha_of "$1/$3/$f")" = "$(sha_of "$2/$3/$f")" ] || return 1
      done
    }
    mkdir -p "$B/c-ident/a/w" "$B/c-ident/b/w" "$B/c-ident/c/w" "$B/c-ident/d/w"
    printf 'pk' >"$B/c-ident/a/w/out.host.xlsx"; printf 'line\n' >"$B/c-ident/a/w/stdout.host.txt"
    cp "$B/c-ident/a/w/out.host.xlsx" "$B/c-ident/a/w/stdout.host.txt" "$B/c-ident/b/w/"
    cp "$B/c-ident/a/w/out.host.xlsx" "$B/c-ident/c/w/"; printf 'line2\n' >"$B/c-ident/c/w/stdout.host.txt"
    cp "$B/c-ident/a/w/stdout.host.txt" "$B/c-ident/d/w/"
    check "control: the planted differing line differs from the original (cmp)" "$(ynnot cmp -s "$B/c-ident/a/w/stdout.host.txt" "$B/c-ident/c/w/stdout.host.txt")"
    check "control: same_row accepts two planted rows the same byte for byte" "$(yn same_row "$B/c-ident/a" "$B/c-ident/b" w xlsx host)"
    check "control: same_row refuses a planted row whose line differs" "$(ynnot same_row "$B/c-ident/a" "$B/c-ident/c" w xlsx host)"
    check "control: same_row refuses a planted row with no output" "$(ynnot same_row "$B/c-ident/a" "$B/c-ident/d" w xlsx host)"
    # prevrec.py <run dir> <record .txt>: the earlier run directory's summaries,
    # every label's in order, against the summary table, the first of three, of
    # that run's committed record (M5 part 5 P4's, carried).
    cat >"$B/prevrec.py" <<'PY'
    import os
    import sys
    
    sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
    run_dir, txt = sys.argv[1:3]
    
    
    def lines(path):
        out = open(path, encoding="utf-8").read().split("\n")
        return out[:-1] if out and out[-1] == "" else out
    
    
    labels = [l for l in ("host", "i686") if os.path.exists("%s/summary.%s.tsv" % (run_dir, l))]
    summary = []
    for label in labels:
        s = lines("%s/summary.%s.tsv" % (run_dir, label))
        summary = summary or [s[0]]
        summary += s[1:]
    tables = "\n".join(lines(txt)).split("\n\n")
    ok = len(labels) == 2 and len(tables) == 3 and tables[0].split("\n") == summary
    print("labels %s; summary rows %d; the record's summary table is the run directory's: %s" % (",".join(labels), len(summary) - 1, "yes" if ok else "no"))
    PY
    echo "command: <work>/prevrec.py <earlier run directory> <its committed record's .txt>; the program:"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/prevrec.py"
    git show "$C:$P2_TXT" >"$B/prev-p2.txt"
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:$P2_TXT; <work>/prevrec.py <corpus>/runs/${P2_RUN_NAME:-none} <it>"
    python3 -I -B "$B/prevrec.py" "$P2_RUN" "$B/prev-p2.txt" >"$B/prevrec-p2.out" 2>&1
    echo "  $(cat "$B/prevrec-p2.out")"
    check "P2's run directory's summaries, both labels, are its committed record's summary table (change NXI)" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -E "is the run directory's: yes\$" "$B/prevrec-p2.out")" = 1 ])"
    sed '2d' "$B/prev-p2.txt" >"$B/c-prev-p2.txt"
    python3 -I -B "$B/prevrec.py" "$P2_RUN" "$B/c-prev-p2.txt" >"$B/c-prevrec-p2.out" 2>&1
    check "control: the same program refuses that record with one summary row dropped" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -E "is the run directory's: no\$" "$B/c-prevrec-p2.out")" = 1 ])"
    NOW_RUN=$RUN_OUT_ROOT/$RUN-chartsheet
    for label in host i686; do
      nrow=0; nsame=0
      : >"$B/ident-$label"
      while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
        nrow=$((nrow + 1))
        printf '    %s %s out %s %s line %s %s\n' "$id" "$label" \
          "$(sha_of "$NOW_RUN/$id/out.$label.$ext" 2>/dev/null)" "$(sha_of "$P2_RUN/$id/out.$label.$ext" 2>/dev/null)" \
          "$(sha_of "$NOW_RUN/$id/stdout.$label.txt" 2>/dev/null)" "$(sha_of "$P2_RUN/$id/stdout.$label.txt" 2>/dev/null)" >>"$B/ident-$label"
        if same_row "$NOW_RUN" "$P2_RUN" "$id" "$ext" "$label"; then nsame=$((nsame + 1)); else echo "    FINDING (an output byte of the sample moved since P2's run; change NXI): $id: $label: the output or the line differs from P2's run"; fi
      done <"$B/order"
      echo "  chartsheet $label: per row, id, label, the output's sha256 now and in P2's run, the line's now and in P2's run:"
      cat "$B/ident-$label"
      echo "  chartsheet $label: rows compared $nrow; identical, output and line, by sha256: $nsame"
      rr_same() { [ "$nrow" = "$manifest_rows" ] && [ "$nsame" = "$nrow" ]; }
      check "chartsheet $label: every row's output and line are byte-identical to P2's run, by sha256, $nsame of $manifest_rows (change NXI)" "$(yn rr_same)"
    done
    rr_first_id=$(head -n 1 "$B/order" | cut -f1)
    rr_first_ext=$(head -n 1 "$B/order" | cut -f2)
    rr_ctl() { same_row "$NOW_RUN" "$P2_RUN" "${rr_first_id}x" "$rr_first_ext" host; }
    check "control: same_row refuses the first workbook's id with a letter appended, which neither run holds" "$(ynnot rr_ctl)"
    echo
    echo "## the openpyxl fixture: written by the pinned image, --charts-sample on it through the runner and --chartsheet-sample on it by the size log's release binaries, both targets, the line and the refusal against P2's run.log (specs/0038 \"Harness runs\", the second fixture; P2 ruling J; changes NXC and NXJ)"
    OPX_IMAGE=localhost/emend-openpyxl:3.1.5-dfsg-2-deb13
    OPX_REC=records/openpyxl-image-2026-10-16.md
    echo "plan (printed before any container of this block runs): one rootless podman run of $OPX_IMAGE, an image already built (no pull, no build, no install), with --network=none and --userns=keep-id, tests/fixtures/openpyxl-ops.xlsx and scripts/openpyxl-ops.py mounted read-only from <repo>, <work>/opx the one writable mount; then the runner and the release binaries over its output under <work>, as for the corpus; nothing needs elevation"
    uid_now=$(id -u)
    rootless_now=$(podman info --format '{{.Host.Security.Rootless}}' 2>/dev/null)
    echo "command: id -u; podman info --format '{{.Host.Security.Rootless}}'"
    echo "  uid $uid_now; rootless ${rootless_now:-none}"
    not_root() { [ "$uid_now" != 0 ]; }
    check "this script runs as an account other than root (change NXC)" "$(yn not_root)"
    not_root_ctl() { local uid_now=0; not_root; }
    check "control: the same check refuses uid 0" "$(ynnot not_root_ctl)"
    is_rootless() { [ "$rootless_now" = true ]; }
    check "podman runs rootless (change NXC)" "$(yn is_rootless)"
    echo "command: podman image exists $OPX_IMAGE"
    check "the pinned openpyxl image is there" "$(yn podman image exists "$OPX_IMAGE")"
    rec_id=$(git show "$C:$OPX_REC" | sed -n 's/^| Image id | `\([0-9a-f]\{64\}\)` |$/\1/p')
    img_id=$(podman image inspect --format '{{.Id}}' "$OPX_IMAGE" 2>/dev/null | sed 's/^sha256://')
    lo_id=$(podman image inspect --format '{{.Id}}' "$IMAGE" 2>/dev/null | sed 's/^sha256://')
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:$OPX_REC, its Image id row; podman image inspect --format '{{.Id}}' $OPX_IMAGE"
    echo "  the record's image id: ${rec_id:-none}; the image's: ${img_id:-none}"
    id_ok() { printf '%s' "$rec_id" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qxE '[0-9a-f]{64}' && [ "$img_id" = "$rec_id" ]; }
    check "the openpyxl image's id is the one $OPX_REC records (change NXC)" "$(yn id_ok)"
    id_ctl() { local img_id=$lo_id; id_ok; }
    check "control: the same check refuses the LibreOffice image's id" "$(ynnot id_ctl)"
    mkdir "$B/opx" || exit 2
    OPX_OUT=$B/opx/chartsheet.xlsx
    echo "command: podman run --rm --network=none --userns=keep-id -v <repo>/tests/fixtures/openpyxl-ops.xlsx:/in/fixture.xlsx:ro -v <work>/opx:/out -v <repo>/scripts/openpyxl-ops.py:/ops.py:ro $OPX_IMAGE python3 -I -B /ops.py chartsheet /in/fixture.xlsx /out/chartsheet.xlsx"
    podman run --rm --network=none --userns=keep-id \
      -v "$MAIN/tests/fixtures/openpyxl-ops.xlsx":/in/fixture.xlsx:ro -v "$B/opx":/out -v "$MAIN/scripts/openpyxl-ops.py":/ops.py:ro "$OPX_IMAGE" \
      python3 -I -B /ops.py chartsheet /in/fixture.xlsx /out/chartsheet.xlsx </dev/null >"$B/opx.stdout" 2>"$B/opx.stderr"
    opx_rc=$?
    echo "  exit $opx_rc; standard error $(wc -c <"$B/opx.stderr") bytes; standard output:"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/opx.stdout"
    opx_ok() {
      [ "$opx_rc" = 0 ] && [ ! -s "$B/opx.stderr" ] && [ "$(count_lines "$B/opx.stdout")" = 1 ] || return 1
      LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE "^openpyxl=3[.]1[.]5${TAB}peak_rss_kb=[1-9][0-9]*\$" "$B/opx.stdout" && [ -s "$OPX_OUT" ]
    }
    check "the op exits 0 with nothing on standard error, its one line openpyxl 3.1.5 and a peak RSS, and writes its output (change NXC)" "$(yn opx_ok)"
    echo "  the output: $(stat -c %s "$OPX_OUT" 2>/dev/null) bytes, sha256 $(sha_of "$OPX_OUT" 2>/dev/null)"
    # The output's check (change NXC): its last <sheet> and the chartsheet its
    # relationship names, read with zipfile and ElementTree; the drawing
    # through the chartsheet's rels part, whose target openpyxl writes as an
    # absolute part name; the workbook root's own start tag, read as text.
    cat >"$B/opxcheck.py" <<'PY'
    """Checks the chartsheet openpyxl's chartsheet op wrote into <workbook>: three
    sheets, the last named Chart with a relationship of the chartsheet type, the
    part it names with its Override of the chartsheet content type and a root
    of chartsheet; the drawing its drawing element names through the part's
    rels: one absoluteAnchor with pos 0,0 and ext 0 by 0, its frame naming one
    chart part holding a barChart; and the workbook root's start tag binding no
    prefix for the relationships namespace. Prints one "name: yes|no" line per
    check, a check that cannot be read "no"; the workbook's text is not
    printed."""
    import posixpath
    import re
    import sys
    import zipfile
    import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
    
    sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
    CS_TYPE = "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.chartsheet+xml"
    REL_NS = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships"
    R = "{%s}id" % REL_NS
    
    
    def local(tag):
        return tag.rsplit("}", 1)[-1]
    
    
    def resolve(base, target):
        if target.startswith("/"):
            return target[1:]
        return posixpath.normpath(posixpath.join(posixpath.dirname(base), target))
    
    
    def rels_of(z, part):
        d, b = posixpath.split(part)
        root = ET.fromstring(z.read(posixpath.join(d, "_rels", b + ".rels")))
        return {r.get("Id"): (r.get("Type") or "", resolve(part, r.get("Target") or ""))
                for r in root if local(r.tag) == "Relationship"}
    
    
    state = {}
    checks = []
    
    
    def check(name, fn):
        try:
            ok = bool(fn())
        except Exception:
            ok = False
        checks.append((name, ok))
    
    
    z = zipfile.ZipFile(sys.argv[1])
    wb = "xl/workbook.xml"
    
    
    def sheets():
        s = [e for c in ET.fromstring(z.read(wb)) if local(c.tag) == "sheets" for e in c]
        state["last"] = s[-1]
        return len(s) == 3 and s[-1].get("name") == "Chart"
    
    
    def sheet_rel():
        kind, part = rels_of(z, wb)[state["last"].get(R)]
        state["part"] = part
        return kind.endswith("/relationships/chartsheet") and part == "xl/chartsheets/sheet1.xml"
    
    
    def override():
        types = ET.fromstring(z.read("[Content_Types].xml"))
        over = [o.get("ContentType") for o in types if local(o.tag) == "Override" and o.get("PartName") == "/" + state["part"]]
        return over == [CS_TYPE]
    
    
    def root_is():
        state["root"] = ET.fromstring(z.read(state["part"]))
        return local(state["root"].tag) == "chartsheet"
    
    
    def drawing_rel():
        el = [c for c in state["root"] if local(c.tag) == "drawing"]
        kind, part = rels_of(z, state["part"])[el[0].get(R)]
        state["drawing"] = part
        return len(el) == 1 and kind.endswith("/relationships/drawing") and part in z.namelist()
    
    
    def one_anchor():
        anchors = list(ET.fromstring(z.read(state["drawing"])))
        state["anchor"] = anchors[0]
        return len(anchors) == 1 and local(anchors[0].tag) == "absoluteAnchor"
    
    
    def pos_zero():
        pos = [c for c in state["anchor"] if local(c.tag) == "pos"]
        return len(pos) == 1 and pos[0].get("x") == "0" and pos[0].get("y") == "0"
    
    
    def ext_zero():
        ext = [c for c in state["anchor"] if local(c.tag) == "ext"]
        return len(ext) == 1 and ext[0].get("cx") == "0" and ext[0].get("cy") == "0"
    
    
    def bar_chart():
        ids = [e.get(R) for e in state["anchor"].iter() if local(e.tag) == "chart"]
        kind, part = rels_of(z, state["drawing"])[ids[0]]
        plot = ET.fromstring(z.read(part))
        return len(ids) == 1 and kind.endswith("/relationships/chart") and any(local(e.tag) == "barChart" for e in plot.iter())
    
    
    def no_prefix():
        text = z.read(wb).decode("utf-8")
        start = re.search(r"<(?:[A-Za-z_][\w.-]*:)?workbook\b[^>]*>", text).group(0)
        return REL_NS not in start
    
    
    check("three sheets, the last named Chart", sheets)
    check("its relationship is of the chartsheet type, naming xl/chartsheets/sheet1.xml", sheet_rel)
    check("its part has one Override, of the chartsheet content type", override)
    check("the part's root is chartsheet", root_is)
    check("its one drawing element names a drawing relationship, its target resolved to an entry", drawing_rel)
    check("the drawing holds one absoluteAnchor", one_anchor)
    check("its pos is 0,0", pos_zero)
    check("its ext is 0 by 0", ext_zero)
    check("its frame names one chart part, which holds a barChart", bar_chart)
    check("the workbook root's start tag binds no prefix for the relationships namespace", no_prefix)
    for name, good in checks:
        print("%s: %s" % (name, "yes" if good else "no"))
    PY
    echo "command: python3 -I -B <work>/opxcheck.py <work>/opx/chartsheet.xlsx; and over the committed fixture tests/fixtures/openpyxl-ops.xlsx (the control); the program:"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/opxcheck.py"
    python3 -I -B "$B/opxcheck.py" "$OPX_OUT" >"$B/opxcheck.out" 2>&1
    echo "  exit: $?"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/opxcheck.out"
    opx_all() { [ "$(count_matches -E ': yes$' "$B/opxcheck.out")" = 10 ] && [ "$(count_matches -E ': no$' "$B/opxcheck.out")" = 0 ]; }
    check "fixture: the op's output holds the chartsheet, its drawing's one absoluteAnchor at 0,0 of ext 0 by 0 and its bar chart, and its workbook root binds no relationships prefix (ten checks; change NXC)" "$(yn opx_all)"
    python3 -I -B "$B/opxcheck.py" tests/fixtures/openpyxl-ops.xlsx >"$B/c-opxcheck.out" 2>&1
    echo "  over the committed fixture, which holds no chartsheet: $(count_matches -E ': no$' "$B/c-opxcheck.out") checks no"
    opx_ctl() { [ "$(count_matches -E ': no$' "$B/c-opxcheck.out")" -ge 6 ]; }
    check "control: the same check finds the committed fixture's workbook holds no such chartsheet (six checks no at least)" "$(yn opx_ctl)"
    # The one-workbook corpus the runner takes with --corpus (change NXC).
    cat >"$B/opxcorpus.py" <<'PY'
    """Copies the workbook given first into corpus/<id>.xlsx in the directory
    given second, and writes manifest.tsv beside corpus there, one row in
    specs/0005's form, <id> the first twelve hex digits of the workbook's
    sha256; the date given third is the row's added column. Prints the id, the
    byte count and the sha256."""
    import hashlib
    import os
    import sys
    
    sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
    MANIFEST_HEADER = ("id\tsha256\tbytes\text\tproducer\tproducer_version\tapp\tsource\ttags\tadded"
                       "\toriginal_name\tnote")
    src, out, date = sys.argv[1:4]
    data = open(src, "rb").read()
    digest = hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()
    ident = digest[:12]
    os.makedirs(os.path.join(out, "corpus"))
    with open(os.path.join(out, "corpus", ident + ".xlsx"), "wb") as f:
        f.write(data)
    row = [ident, digest, str(len(data)), "xlsx", "openpyxl", "3.1.5", "openpyxl", "generated", "fixture",
           date, "openpyxl-chartsheet.xlsx", "fictional"]
    with open(os.path.join(out, "manifest.tsv"), "w", encoding="utf-8", newline="\n") as f:
        f.write(MANIFEST_HEADER + "\n" + "\t".join(row) + "\n")
    print("%s\t%d\t%s" % (ident, len(data), digest))
    PY
    echo "command: python3 -I -B <work>/opxcorpus.py <work>/opx/chartsheet.xlsx <work>/opxcorpus $DATE; the program:"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/opxcorpus.py"
    python3 -I -B "$B/opxcorpus.py" "$OPX_OUT" "$B/opxcorpus" "$DATE" >"$B/opxcorpus.out" 2>"$B/opxcorpus.err" </dev/null
    oc_rc=$?
    OPX_ID=$(cut -f1 "$B/opxcorpus.out")
    OPX_IN=$B/opxcorpus/corpus/$OPX_ID.xlsx
    echo "  exit: $oc_rc; standard error $(wc -c <"$B/opxcorpus.err") bytes; the fixture: id $OPX_ID, $(cut -f2 "$B/opxcorpus.out") bytes, sha256 $(cut -f3 "$B/opxcorpus.out")"
    oc_ok() { [ "$oc_rc" = 0 ] && [ ! -s "$B/opxcorpus.err" ] && cmp -s "$OPX_IN" "$OPX_OUT"; }
    check "the corpus program exits 0, writes nothing to its standard error, and its copy is the op's output byte for byte" "$(yn oc_ok)"
    OPX_ENTRIES=$(python3 -I -B -c 'import sys, zipfile; print(len(zipfile.ZipFile(sys.argv[1]).namelist()))' "$OPX_IN" 2>/dev/null)
    echo "  the fixture's entries: ${OPX_ENTRIES:-none}"
    # --charts-sample through the runner, each target into <work>/opxrun-charts.
    FO=$B/opxrun-charts
    for label in host i686; do
      var=PT_$label; PT=${!var}; var=XD_$label; XD=${!var}
      echo "command: TMPDIR=<work>/tmp-run scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label $label --passthrough <work>/bin/$label/emend-copy --xlsx-diff <work>/bin/$label/xlsx-diff --corpus <work>/opxcorpus --out <work>/opxrun-charts --libreoffice $IMAGE --lo-timeout $LO_TIMEOUT_S --timeout 300 --tool-arg --charts-sample"
      TMPDIR=$RUNTMP scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label "$label" --passthrough "$PT" --xlsx-diff "$XD" --corpus "$B/opxcorpus" --out "$FO" \
        --libreoffice "$IMAGE" --lo-timeout "$LO_TIMEOUT_S" --timeout 300 --tool-arg --charts-sample \
        >"$B/opx-charts-$label.stdout" 2>"$B/opx-charts-$label.stderr" </dev/null
      frc=$?
      echo "  exit $frc; stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$B/opx-charts-$label.stderr")"
      sed 's/^/    /' "$B/opx-charts-$label.stdout"
      FSUM=$FO/summary.$label.tsv
      opx_row_ok() { [ "$frc" = 0 ] && [ ! -s "$B/opx-charts-$label.stderr" ] && [ "$(awk 'NR > 1' "$FSUM" | wc -l)" = 1 ] \
        && [ "$(count_where "$FSUM" outcome ok)" = 1 ] && [ "$(count_where "$FSUM" lo ok)" = 1 ] \
        && [ "$(count_where "$FSUM" lo_in ok)" = 1 ] && [ "$(count_where "$FSUM" leftover no)" = 1 ]; }
      check "fixture charts $label: the run exits 0 with an empty stderr, its one row ok, the input and the output opening in LibreOffice (lo_in and lo ok), nothing left over" "$(yn opx_row_ok)"
      e=$(cat "$FO/$OPX_ID/stdout.$label.txt")
      printf '%s\n' "$e" >"$B/opxline-$label"
      echo "  the line: $(printf '%s' "$e" | tr '\t' ' ')"
    done
    check "fixture charts: both targets printed the same line" "$(yn cmp -s "$B/opxline-host" "$B/opxline-i686")"
    check "fixture charts: the output is the same on both targets, byte for byte" "$(yn cmp -s "$FO/$OPX_ID/out.host.xlsx" "$FO/$OPX_ID/out.i686.xlsx")"
    OL=$(cat "$B/opxline-host")
    opx_charts_ok() { [ "$(printf '%s\n' "$OL" | cut -f1)" = charts ] && [ "$(kv "$OL" sheets)" = 3 ] && [ "$(kv "$OL" charts)" = 1 ] \
      && [ "$(kv "$OL" series)" = 1 ] && [ "$(kv "$OL" plots)" = 1 ] && [ "$(kv "$OL" kind_bar)" = 1 ] && [ "$(kv "$OL" anchor_abs)" = 1 ]; }
    check "fixture charts: the line reads the chartsheet's chart through its absoluteAnchor (sheets 3, two worksheets and the chartsheet; charts 1; series 1; plots 1, a bar; anchor_abs 1)" "$(yn opx_charts_ok)"
    opx_charts_ctl() { local OL; OL=$(cat "$B/opxline-host" | sed 's/\tcharts=1\t/\tcharts=0\t/'); opx_charts_ok; }
    check "control: the same check refuses the line with charts 0" "$(ynnot opx_charts_ctl)"
    FE=$FO/entries.host.tsv
    n_opx_rows=$(awk 'NR > 1' "$FE" | wc -l)
    n_opx_same=$(awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next } $k["status"] == "identical" && $k["flags"] == ""' "$FE" | wc -l)
    echo "  the charts sample's entry rows: $n_opx_rows; identical and unflagged: $n_opx_same; the fixture's entries: ${OPX_ENTRIES:-none}"
    opx_same() { [ -n "$OPX_ENTRIES" ] && [ "$n_opx_rows" = "$OPX_ENTRIES" ] && [ "$n_opx_same" = "$OPX_ENTRIES" ]; }
    check "fixture charts: the input written back unedited, each of its entries identical and unflagged" "$(yn opx_same)"
    opx_same_ctl() { local n_opx_same=$((n_opx_same - 1)); opx_same; }
    check "control: the same check refuses one entry fewer identical" "$(ynnot opx_same_ctl)"
    # --chartsheet-sample by the release binaries, each target, into
    # <work>/opx-refused, which must stay empty (P2 ruling J).
    NO_PREFIX_LINE="error: the workbook root binds no prefix for the relationships namespace"
    git show "$C:crates/emend/src/package.rs" >"$B/package.rs"
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:crates/emend/src/package.rs; count_matches -F the message's Error::Package literal"
    echo "  the message's literal in the phase commit's package.rs: $(count_matches -F "Error::Package(\"${NO_PREFIX_LINE#error: }\")" "$B/package.rs") (NO_RELATIONSHIPS_PREFIX)"
    check "the refusal's message, read apart, is package.rs's NO_RELATIONSHIPS_PREFIX literal, once (change NXC)" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -F "Error::Package(\"${NO_PREFIX_LINE#error: }\")" "$B/package.rs")" = 1 ])"
    mkdir "$B/opx-refused" || exit 2
    # refused_ok <stem> <output>: exit 2, nothing on standard output, the one
    # line of the message on standard error, and no output written.
    refused_ok() { [ "$(cat "$1.rc")" = 2 ] && [ ! -s "$1.stdout" ] && [ "$(count_lines "$1.stderr")" = 1 ] && [ "$(cat "$1.stderr")" = "$NO_PREFIX_LINE" ] && [ ! -e "$2" ]; }
    for label in host i686; do
      var=PT_$label; PT=${!var}
      echo "command: TMPDIR=<work>/tmp-run <work>/bin/$label/emend-copy <work>/opxcorpus/corpus/$OPX_ID.xlsx <work>/opx-refused/out.$label.xlsx --chartsheet-sample"
      TMPDIR=$RUNTMP "$PT" "$OPX_IN" "$B/opx-refused/out.$label.xlsx" --chartsheet-sample >"$B/opx-refused-$label.stdout" 2>"$B/opx-refused-$label.stderr" </dev/null
      echo "$?" >"$B/opx-refused-$label.rc"
      echo "  exit $(cat "$B/opx-refused-$label.rc"); standard output $(wc -c <"$B/opx-refused-$label.stdout") bytes; standard error:"
      sed 's/^/    /' "$B/opx-refused-$label.stderr"
      check "fixture chartsheet $label: exit 2, nothing on standard output, the one line \"$NO_PREFIX_LINE\" on standard error, no output file (P2 ruling J; change NXC)" "$(yn refused_ok "$B/opx-refused-$label" "$B/opx-refused/out.$label.xlsx")"
    done
    check "fixture chartsheet: both targets wrote the same standard error" "$(yn cmp -s "$B/opx-refused-host.stderr" "$B/opx-refused-i686.stderr")"
    refused_empty() { [ -z "$(find "$B/opx-refused" -mindepth 1)" ]; }
    check "fixture chartsheet: <work>/opx-refused holds nothing after the two refusals, no output and no temporary" "$(yn refused_empty)"
    printf '0\n' >"$B/c-acc.rc"; printf 'chartsheet\tpart_length=25\n' >"$B/c-acc.stdout"; : >"$B/c-acc.stderr"; printf 'pk' >"$B/c-acc-out.xlsx"
    check "control: refused_ok refuses a planted accepted run (exit 0, a line, an output)" "$(ynnot refused_ok "$B/c-acc" "$B/c-acc-out.xlsx")"
    printf '2\n' >"$B/c-other.rc"; : >"$B/c-other.stdout"; printf 'error: no such part\n' >"$B/c-other.stderr"
    check "control: refused_ok refuses a planted refusal with another message" "$(ynnot refused_ok "$B/c-other" "$B/c-other-out.xlsx")"
    n_left=$(find "$RUNTMP" -mindepth 1 | wc -l)
    check "fixture: the runs' TMPDIR is empty after the runs" "$(yn [ "$n_left" = 0 ])"
    # Change NXJ: the fresh fixture's charts line and refusal against what P2's
    # committed run.log prints (the op writes a new file each run, its zip
    # times and properties the run's, so the fixture itself is not P2's; its
    # line, counts only, and the refusal are).
    git show "$C:records/logs/m6p1-p2/run.log" >"$B/p2-run.log"
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:records/logs/m6p1-p2/run.log (sha256 $(sha_of "$B/p2-run.log")): its '  the line: ' lines, the charts sample's line on each label, and its '    error: ' lines, the refusal's standard error on each label, each in its order, host then i686"
    LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^  the line: charts ' "$B/p2-run.log" | sed 's/^  the line: //' >"$B/p2-lines"
    LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^    error: ' "$B/p2-run.log" | sed 's/^    //' >"$B/p2-errors"
    echo "  lines read: $(count_lines "$B/p2-lines"); error lines read: $(count_lines "$B/p2-errors")"
    check "P2's run.log prints two charts lines and two refusal lines, host then i686 (change NXJ)" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/p2-lines")$(count_lines "$B/p2-errors")" = 22 ])"
    n_line_same=0
    k=0
    for label in host i686; do
      k=$((k + 1))
      now_line=$(tr '\t' ' ' <"$B/opxline-$label")
      then_line=$(sed -n "${k}p" "$B/p2-lines")
      now_err=$(cat "$B/opx-refused-$label.stderr")
      then_err=$(sed -n "${k}p" "$B/p2-errors")
      line_same() { [ -n "$then_line" ] && [ "$now_line" = "$then_line" ] && [ -n "$then_err" ] && [ "$now_err" = "$then_err" ]; }
      if line_same; then n_line_same=$((n_line_same + 1)); fi
      check "fixture $label: the charts line and the refusal's standard error are the ones P2's run.log prints for $label (change NXJ)" "$(yn line_same)"
    done
    line_ctl() { local now_line; now_line=$(tr '\t' ' ' <"$B/opxline-host" | sed 's/ charts=1 / charts=0 /'); line_same; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the line with charts 0" "$(ynnot line_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "## P2's own openpyxl fixture, from P2's kept working directory, the two samples on it once more by the size log's release binaries, both targets, against P2's kept outputs by sha256 (specs/0038 \"P3\" and ruling M; change NXJ)"
    P2_OPX_SHA=$(sed -n -E 's/^  the output: [0-9]+ bytes, sha256 ([0-9a-f]{64})$/\1/p' "$B/p2-run.log")
    echo "  the op output's sha256 P2's run.log prints: ${P2_OPX_SHA:-none}"
    check "P2's run.log prints the op output's sha256 once (change NXJ)" "$(yn [ "$(printf '%s\n' "$P2_OPX_SHA" | count_matches -E '^[0-9a-f]{64}$' /dev/stdin)" = 1 ])"
    : >"$B/p2-workdirs"
    for d in "$P2_PHASE"/tmp/tmp.*; do
      if [ -f "$d/opx/chartsheet.xlsx" ] && [ "$(sha_of "$d/opx/chartsheet.xlsx")" = "$P2_OPX_SHA" ]; then printf '%s\n' "$d" >>"$B/p2-workdirs"; fi
    done
    echo "command: sha256sum <p2phase>/tmp/tmp.*/opx/chartsheet.xlsx, those whose sha256 is P2's printed one:"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/p2-workdirs"
    check "exactly one of P2's kept working directories holds the op output P2's run.log hashed (change NXJ)" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/p2-workdirs")" = 1 ])"
    P2W=$(head -n 1 "$B/p2-workdirs")
    P2_OPX_ID=${P2_OPX_SHA:0:12}
    p2w_ok() {
      local label
      [ -n "$P2W" ] && [ "$(sha_of "$P2W/opxcorpus/corpus/$P2_OPX_ID.xlsx")" = "$P2_OPX_SHA" ] && [ -f "$P2W/opxcorpus/manifest.tsv" ] || return 1
      for label in host i686; do
        [ -f "$P2W/opxrun-charts/$P2_OPX_ID/out.$label.xlsx" ] && [ -f "$P2W/opxrun-charts/$P2_OPX_ID/stdout.$label.txt" ] || return 1
        [ -f "$P2W/opx-refused-$label.stderr" ] && [ -f "$P2W/opx-refused-$label.rc" ] && [ -f "$P2W/opx-refused-$label.stdout" ] || return 1
      done
    }
    check "it holds P2's one-workbook corpus of that file, the charts sample's outputs and lines and the refusals' files, both labels (change NXJ)" "$(yn p2w_ok)"
    cp -r "$P2W/opxcorpus" "$B/p2opxcorpus"
    echo "command: cp -r <p2work>/opxcorpus <work>/p2opxcorpus (<p2work> is the directory found above, under <p2phase>/tmp, read only)"
    p2c_ok() { cmp -s "$P2W/opxcorpus/manifest.tsv" "$B/p2opxcorpus/manifest.tsv" && cmp -s "$P2W/opxcorpus/corpus/$P2_OPX_ID.xlsx" "$B/p2opxcorpus/corpus/$P2_OPX_ID.xlsx"; }
    check "the copy is P2's corpus, its manifest and its workbook byte for byte" "$(yn p2c_ok)"
    P2O=$B/p2opxrun-charts
    mkdir "$B/p2opx-refused" || exit 2
    n_p2_same=0
    for label in host i686; do
      var=PT_$label; PT=${!var}; var=XD_$label; XD=${!var}
      echo "command: TMPDIR=<work>/tmp-run scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label $label --passthrough <work>/bin/$label/emend-copy --xlsx-diff <work>/bin/$label/xlsx-diff --corpus <work>/p2opxcorpus --out <work>/p2opxrun-charts --libreoffice $IMAGE --lo-timeout $LO_TIMEOUT_S --timeout 300 --tool-arg --charts-sample"
      TMPDIR=$RUNTMP scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label "$label" --passthrough "$PT" --xlsx-diff "$XD" --corpus "$B/p2opxcorpus" --out "$P2O" \
        --libreoffice "$IMAGE" --lo-timeout "$LO_TIMEOUT_S" --timeout 300 --tool-arg --charts-sample \
        >"$B/p2opx-charts-$label.stdout" 2>"$B/p2opx-charts-$label.stderr" </dev/null
      prc=$?
      echo "  exit $prc; stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$B/p2opx-charts-$label.stderr")"
      sed 's/^/    /' "$B/p2opx-charts-$label.stdout"
      PSUM=$P2O/summary.$label.tsv
      p2_row_ok() { [ "$prc" = 0 ] && [ ! -s "$B/p2opx-charts-$label.stderr" ] && [ "$(awk 'NR > 1' "$PSUM" | wc -l)" = 1 ] \
        && [ "$(count_where "$PSUM" outcome ok)" = 1 ] && [ "$(count_where "$PSUM" lo ok)" = 1 ] \
        && [ "$(count_where "$PSUM" lo_in ok)" = 1 ] && [ "$(count_where "$PSUM" leftover no)" = 1 ]; }
      check "P2's fixture charts $label: the run exits 0 with an empty stderr, its one row ok, lo_in and lo ok, nothing left over" "$(yn p2_row_ok)"
      echo "  out.$label.xlsx: $(sha_of "$P2O/$P2_OPX_ID/out.$label.xlsx" 2>/dev/null) now, $(sha_of "$P2W/opxrun-charts/$P2_OPX_ID/out.$label.xlsx") in P2's run; stdout.$label.txt: $(sha_of "$P2O/$P2_OPX_ID/stdout.$label.txt" 2>/dev/null) now, $(sha_of "$P2W/opxrun-charts/$P2_OPX_ID/stdout.$label.txt") in P2's run"
      if same_row "$P2O" "$P2W/opxrun-charts" "$P2_OPX_ID" xlsx "$label"; then n_p2_same=$((n_p2_same + 1)); fi
      check "P2's fixture charts $label: the output and the line are byte-identical to P2's, by sha256 (change NXJ)" "$(yn same_row "$P2O" "$P2W/opxrun-charts" "$P2_OPX_ID" xlsx "$label")"
      echo "command: TMPDIR=<work>/tmp-run <work>/bin/$label/emend-copy <work>/p2opxcorpus/corpus/$P2_OPX_ID.xlsx <work>/p2opx-refused/out.$label.xlsx --chartsheet-sample"
      TMPDIR=$RUNTMP "$PT" "$B/p2opxcorpus/corpus/$P2_OPX_ID.xlsx" "$B/p2opx-refused/out.$label.xlsx" --chartsheet-sample >"$B/p2opx-refused-$label.stdout" 2>"$B/p2opx-refused-$label.stderr" </dev/null
      echo "$?" >"$B/p2opx-refused-$label.rc"
      echo "  exit $(cat "$B/p2opx-refused-$label.rc") (P2's $(cat "$P2W/opx-refused-$label.rc")); standard output $(wc -c <"$B/p2opx-refused-$label.stdout") bytes; standard error sha256 $(sha_of "$B/p2opx-refused-$label.stderr") now, $(sha_of "$P2W/opx-refused-$label.stderr") in P2's run"
      p2_refused_same() { refused_ok "$B/p2opx-refused-$label" "$B/p2opx-refused/out.$label.xlsx" && cmp -s "$B/p2opx-refused-$label.rc" "$P2W/opx-refused-$label.rc" \
        && cmp -s "$B/p2opx-refused-$label.stdout" "$P2W/opx-refused-$label.stdout" && cmp -s "$B/p2opx-refused-$label.stderr" "$P2W/opx-refused-$label.stderr"; }
      check "P2's fixture chartsheet $label: refused as P2's, exit 2 and no output, its exit, standard output and standard error byte-identical to P2's (P2 ruling J; change NXJ)" "$(yn p2_refused_same)"
    done
    check "P2's fixture: both labels' outputs and lines byte-identical to P2's ($n_p2_same of 2; change NXJ)" "$(yn [ "$n_p2_same" = 2 ])"
    mkdir -p "$B/c-p2opx/$P2_OPX_ID"
    cp "$P2O/$P2_OPX_ID/stdout.host.txt" "$B/c-p2opx/$P2_OPX_ID/"
    cp "$FO/$OPX_ID/out.host.xlsx" "$B/c-p2opx/$P2_OPX_ID/out.host.xlsx"
    check "control: same_row refuses a planted row holding the fresh fixture's output under P2's fixture's id" "$(ynnot same_row "$B/c-p2opx" "$P2W/opxrun-charts" "$P2_OPX_ID" xlsx host)"
    check "control: the fresh fixture's output is not P2's fixture's (the op writes a new file each run)" "$(ynnot cmp -s "$FO/$OPX_ID/out.host.xlsx" "$P2O/$P2_OPX_ID/out.host.xlsx")"
    p2_refused_empty() { [ -z "$(find "$B/p2opx-refused" -mindepth 1)" ]; }
    check "P2's fixture chartsheet: <work>/p2opx-refused holds nothing after the two refusals" "$(yn p2_refused_empty)"
    n_left2=$(find "$RUNTMP" -mindepth 1 | wc -l)
    check "P2's fixture: the runs' TMPDIR is empty after the runs" "$(yn [ "$n_left2" = 0 ])"
    
    echo
    if [ "$RUN_SKIP_KEEP" = yes ]; then
    echo "## the keep and the open check: SKIPPED (RUN_SKIP_KEEP=yes, a dry run)"
    else
    echo "## the host keep regenerated (change NSF: M3 part 7 P5's form, one cargo test; carried)"
    mkdir "$KEEP" || exit 2
    echo "command: EMEND_KEEP_DIR=<keep> cargo test --workspace (host; CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/main)"
    EMEND_KEEP_DIR=$KEEP cargo test --workspace >"$B/keep.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
    rc=$?
    echo "  exit: $rc"
    LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^ *Running |^ *Doc-tests |^test result: ' "$B/keep.out" | sed 's/^ */    /'
    failed=$(awk '/^test result: / { for (i = 1; i < NF; i++) if ($(i + 1) ~ /^failed;$/) n += $i } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/keep.out")
    passed=$(awk '/^test result: / { for (i = 1; i < NF; i++) if ($(i + 1) ~ /^passed;$/) n += $i } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/keep.out")
    echo "  passed $passed; failed $failed"
    check "the tests with the keep set exit 0" "$(yn [ "$rc" = 0 ])"
    check "no test failed" "$(yn [ "$failed" = 0 ])"
    echo "  files in the keep: $(find "$KEEP" -type f | wc -l); entries that are not regular files: $(find "$KEEP" -mindepth 1 ! -type f | wc -l)"
    (cd "$KEEP" && find . -mindepth 1 -printf '%P\n' | LC_ALL=C sort) >"$B/host.files"
    nfiles=$(count_lines "$B/host.files")
    n_in=$(count_matches -E '\.in\.xlsx$' "$B/host.files")
    n_out=$(count_matches -E '\.out\.xlsx$' "$B/host.files")
    n_other=$(count_matches -vE '^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+\.[0-9]+\.(in|out)\.xlsx$' "$B/host.files")
    LC_ALL=C sed -nE 's/^(.*)\.in\.xlsx$/\1/p' "$B/host.files" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/pair.names"
    LC_ALL=C sed -nE 's/^(.*)\.out\.xlsx$/\1/p' "$B/host.files" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/pair.out.names"
    echo "  .in.xlsx $n_in; .out.xlsx $n_out; names not of the form <test>.<n>.in|out.xlsx: $n_other"
    all_pairs() { [ "$n_in" = "$n_out" ] && [ "$((n_in * 2))" = "$nfiles" ] && [ "$n_other" = 0 ] && cmp -s "$B/pair.names" "$B/pair.out.names"; }
    check "the keep holds only whole pairs named <test>.<n>" "$(yn all_pairs)"
    NPAIRS=$n_in
    (cd "$KEEP" && find . -type f -printf '%P\t%s\n' | LC_ALL=C sort) >"$B/keep.listing"
    echo "  the host keep's listing: pairs $(count_matches -E "[.]in[.]xlsx${TAB}" "$B/keep.listing"); files $(count_lines "$B/keep.listing"); listing sha256 $(sha_of "$B/keep.listing")"
    check "the host keep's pairs times two equals its files (keep_pairs_ok)" "$(yn keep_pairs_ok "$B/keep.listing")"
    
    echo
    echo "## the host keep against P2's committed open-check record, named by its record commit, the base, the last to add one (change NXK)"
    PREV_TXT=$(git show --name-only --format= "$PREV_OPEN_REC" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^records/[a-z0-9]+-open-.*[.]txt$')
    echo "command: git show --name-only --format= <P2's record commit>, the open-check .txt it added; git show <phase commit>:<it>"
    echo "  the record: $PREV_TXT (sha256 $(git show "$C:$PREV_TXT" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1))"
    check "the named record commit added exactly one open-check .txt" "$(yn [ "$(printf '%s\n' "$PREV_TXT" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 1 ])"
    no_later_open() { [ -z "$(git log --format=%H "$PREV_OPEN_REC..$C" -- 'records/*-open-*.txt')" ]; }
    check "no commit after it adds an open-check record, so it is the last committed" "$(yn no_later_open)"
    git show "$C:$PREV_TXT" >"$B/prev.txt"
    while IFS= read -r t; do
      printf '%s\t%s\t%s\t%s\t%s\n' "$t" "$(stat -c %s "$KEEP/$t.in.xlsx")" "$(sha_of "$KEEP/$t.in.xlsx")" \
        "$(stat -c %s "$KEEP/$t.out.xlsx")" "$(sha_of "$KEEP/$t.out.xlsx")"
    done <"$B/pair.names" >"$B/keep.rows"
    tail -n +2 "$B/prev.txt" | cut -f1-5 | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/prev.rows"
    LC_ALL=C sort "$B/keep.rows" >"$B/keep.sorted"
    n_prev=$(count_lines "$B/prev.rows")
    n_kept_prev=$(LC_ALL=C comm -12 "$B/prev.rows" "$B/keep.sorted" | count_lines /dev/stdin)
    cut -f1 "$B/prev.rows" >"$B/prev.names"
    LC_ALL=C comm -13 "$B/prev.names" <(cut -f1 "$B/keep.sorted") >"$B/new.pairs"
    LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/prev.names" <(cut -f1 "$B/keep.sorted") >"$B/gone.pairs"
    echo "  rows: the regenerated keep $(count_lines "$B/keep.rows"), the record $n_prev; its rows found in the keep with the same name, bytes and both sha256s: $n_kept_prev"
    echo "  pairs in the keep and not in the record: $(count_lines "$B/new.pairs"); in the record and not in the keep: $(count_lines "$B/gone.pairs")"
    sed 's/^/    new: /' "$B/new.pairs"
    LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/prev.rows" "$B/keep.sorted" | cut -f1 >"$B/changed.pairs"
    echo "  pairs of the record whose bytes differ in the keep: $(count_lines "$B/changed.pairs")"
    sed 's/^/    changed: /' "$B/changed.pairs"
    check "no pair of the record is gone" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/gone.pairs")" = 0 ])"
    check "every pair of the record is in the keep, unchanged or changed ($n_kept_prev + $(count_lines "$B/changed.pairs") = $n_prev)" "$(yn [ "$((n_kept_prev + $(count_lines "$B/changed.pairs")))" = "$n_prev" ])"
    # Change NXK: the new pairs this phase's tests write: none, P3 adding and
    # editing no test.
    : >"$B/want-new.pairs"
    echo "  the new pairs expected: $(count_lines "$B/want-new.pairs") (change NXK)"
    new_exact() { cmp -s "$B/new.pairs" "$B/want-new.pairs"; }
    check "the new pairs are exactly the $(count_lines "$B/want-new.pairs") this phase's tests write, none, by name (change NXK)" "$(yn new_exact)"
    new_ctl() { { cat "$B/want-new.pairs"; printf '%s\n' zzz_planted_test.1; } >"$B/c-new.pairs"; cmp -s "$B/new.pairs" "$B/c-new.pairs"; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the list with one planted pair more" "$(ynnot new_ctl)"
    check "no pair of the record changed its bytes (change NWU)" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/changed.pairs")" = 0 ])"
    changed_ctl() { printf '%s\n' other.1 >"$B/c-changed.pairs"; [ "$(count_lines "$B/c-changed.pairs")" = 0 ]; }
    check "control: the same count refuses one planted changed pair" "$(ynnot changed_ctl)"
    echo "command: the #[test] functions added or whose body is edited since the named record commit, and those of a .rs file whose text outside its tests differs, from the two commits' sources of every .rs file git diff --name-only <named record commit> <phase commit> names: <work>/edited.py, below (change NSG)"
    cat >"$B/edited.py" <<'PY'
    """The #[test] functions whose body differs between two commits, or that
    the second adds: each file's text at both commits (git show), every
    function after a #[test] attribute (other attributes allowed between), its
    body from the fn line to the first line that is a lone closing brace in
    column one. Prints one test name per line; with a third argument
    --fixtures, instead every test whose body names an item (const,
    static, fn, struct, enum, type or mod at column one) whose lines
    outside the test bodies differ between the two commits (change
    NSG)."""
    import collections
    import re
    import subprocess
    import sys
    
    base, head = sys.argv[1:3]
    TEST = re.compile(r"#\[test\]\s*(?:#\[[^\]]*\]\s*)*fn\s+([A-Za-z0-9_]+)")
    
    
    def show(rev, path):
        run = subprocess.run(["git", "show", "%s:%s" % (rev, path)], capture_output=True)
        return run.stdout.decode() if run.returncode == 0 else ""
    
    
    def tests(text):
        out = {}
        for m in TEST.finditer(text):
            end = text.find("\n}\n", m.start())
            out[m.group(1)] = text[m.start():end if end >= 0 else len(text)]
        return out
    
    
    names = subprocess.run(["git", "diff", "--name-only", base, head, "--", "*.rs"],
                           capture_output=True, check=True).stdout.decode().split()
    ITEM = re.compile(r"^(?:pub(?:\([^)]*\))?\s+)?(?:const|static|fn|struct|enum|type|mod)\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)")
    
    
    def outside(text):
        out, at = [], 0
        for m in TEST.finditer(text):
            end = text.find("\n}\n", m.start())
            end = len(text) if end < 0 else end + 3
            if m.start() >= at:
                out.append(text[at:m.start()])
                at = end
        out.append(text[at:])
        return "".join(out)
    
    
    def changed_items(before_text, after_text):
        found = set()
        for text, other in ((after_text, before_text), (before_text, after_text)):
            others = collections.Counter(outside(other).split("\n"))
            current = None
            for line in outside(text).split("\n"):
                m = ITEM.match(line)
                if m:
                    current = m.group(1)
                if others[line] > 0:
                    others[line] -= 1
                elif current is not None:
                    found.add(current)
        return found
    
    
    edited = set()
    fixture = set()
    for path in names:
        before_text, after_text = show(base, path), show(head, path)
        before, after = tests(before_text), tests(after_text)
        for name, body in after.items():
            if before.get(name) != body:
                edited.add(name)
        items = changed_items(before_text, after_text)
        for name, body in after.items():
            if any(re.search(r"\b%s\b" % re.escape(i), body) for i in items):
                fixture.add(name)
    for name in sorted(fixture if sys.argv[3:] == ["--fixtures"] else edited):
        print(name)
    PY
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/edited.py"
    python3 -I -B "$B/edited.py" "$PREV_OPEN_REC" "$C" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/edited.tests"
    python3 -I -B "$B/edited.py" "$PREV_OPEN_REC" "$C" --fixtures | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/fixture.tests"
    LC_ALL=C sort -u "$B/edited.tests" "$B/fixture.tests" >"$B/touched.tests"
    sed 's/^/    added or edited test: /' "$B/edited.tests"
    sed 's/^/    test of a file whose text outside its tests differs: /' "$B/fixture.tests"
    sed -E 's/\.[0-9]+$//; s/^.*\.//' "$B/new.pairs" | LC_ALL=C sort -u >"$B/new.tests"
    sed -E 's/\.[0-9]+$//; s/^.*\.//' "$B/changed.pairs" | LC_ALL=C sort -u >"$B/changed.tests"
    echo "  tests with a new pair: $(count_lines "$B/new.tests"); tests with a changed pair: $(count_lines "$B/changed.tests"); tests added or edited: $(count_lines "$B/edited.tests"); tests of a file whose text outside its tests differs: $(count_lines "$B/fixture.tests")"
    check "no test is added or edited since the named record commit: P3 adds and edits none (change NXK)" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/edited.tests")" = 0 ])"
    echo "command: <work>/edited.py <named record commit>~5 <named record commit>~1, P2's own range, P1's record commit to P2's phase commit (the control)"
    python3 -I -B "$B/edited.py" "$PREV_OPEN_REC~5" "$PREV_OPEN_REC~1" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/c-edited.tests"
    sed 's/^/    added or edited test: /' "$B/c-edited.tests"
    edited_ctl() { [ "$(cat "$B/c-edited.tests")" = a_chartsheet_renamed_and_moved_in_the_write_that_added_it_is_written_so ]; }
    check "control: the same program over P2's own range finds the carry's test alone, so the list is read (change NXK)" "$(yn edited_ctl)"
    new_from_edited() { [ "$(LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/new.tests" "$B/edited.tests" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 0 ]; }
    check "every new pair is kept by a test added or edited since the record" "$(yn new_from_edited)"
    changed_from_touched() { [ "$(LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/changed.tests" "$B/touched.tests" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 0 ]; }
    check "every changed pair of the record is kept by a test edited since it, or of a file whose fixtures or helpers changed (change NSG)" "$(yn changed_from_touched)"
    printf 'zzz_not_an_edited_test\n' | LC_ALL=C sort -m - "$B/new.tests" >"$B/c-new.tests"
    new_ctl() { [ "$(LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/c-new.tests" "$B/edited.tests" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same comparison finds a pair of a test not added or edited" "$(yn new_ctl)"
    printf 'zzz_not_a_touched_test\n' | LC_ALL=C sort -m - "$B/changed.tests" >"$B/c-changed.tests"
    touched_ctl() { [ "$(LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/c-changed.tests" "$B/touched.tests" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same comparison finds a changed pair of a test neither edited nor of a changed file" "$(yn touched_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "## scripts/edit-open-check.sh on the host keep (specs/0018 \"Harness runs\": every phase's run log runs it over its keep)"
    mkdir "$B/tmp"
    # The open check's own TMPDIR, its device beside the runs' and the corpus
    # directory's.
    dev_open=$(stat -c %d "$B/tmp")
    echo "command: stat -c %d <work>/tmp <work>/tmp-run <corpus>/corpus /proc"
    echo "  device of the open check's TMPDIR (<work>/tmp): $dev_open; of the runs' TMPDIR (<work>/tmp-run): $(stat -c %d "$RUNTMP"); of the corpus directory (<corpus>/corpus): $dev_corpus; of /proc (the control): $dev_proc"
    check "the open check's TMPDIR and the corpus directory are on one device" "$(yn [ "$dev_open" = "$dev_corpus" ])"
    check "control: the same comparison tells /proc's device from the open check's TMPDIR's" "$(yn [ "$dev_proc" != "$dev_open" ])"
    echo "command: TMPDIR=<work>/tmp scripts/edit-open-check.sh --keep <keep> --libreoffice $IMAGE --out <scripts>/out/records --stem $STEM_OPEN"
    TMPDIR=$B/tmp scripts/edit-open-check.sh --keep "$KEEP" --libreoffice "$IMAGE" --out "$RECORDS" --stem "$STEM_OPEN" \
      >"$B/oc.stdout" 2>"$B/oc.stderr" </dev/null
    oc_rc=$?
    echo "  exit: $oc_rc"
    echo "  stdout:"; sed 's/^/    /' "$B/oc.stdout"
    echo "  stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$B/oc.stderr")"
    check "the script exits 0 (no finding, no check errored)" "$(yn [ "$oc_rc" = 0 ])"
    check "its stderr is empty" "$(yn [ ! -s "$B/oc.stderr" ])"
    echo "  the reasons the script kept (its reasons directory under <work>/tmp), one line per refused side:"
    find "$B/tmp" -name '*-reason.txt' | LC_ALL=C sort | while IFS= read -r f; do echo "    ${f#"$B/tmp/"}: $(cat "$f")"; done
    TXT=$RECORDS/$STEM_OPEN.txt
    MD=$RECORDS/$STEM_OPEN.md
    TXT_HEADER=$(git show "$C:scripts/edit-open-check.sh" | sed -n "s/^readonly TXT_HEADER=\\$'\\(.*\\)'\$/\\1/p" | sed 's/\\t/\t/g')
    check "the .txt's header is the script's TXT_HEADER, read from the phase commit (nine columns)" "$(yn [ "$(head -n 1 "$TXT")" = "$TXT_HEADER" ])"
    tail -n +2 "$TXT" | cut -f1-5 >"$B/txt.rows"
    nrow_same=$(paste -d'\n' "$B/keep.rows" "$B/txt.rows" | awk 'NR % 2 == 1 { a = $0; next } a == $0 { n++ } END { print n + 0 }')
    echo "  rows: the keep $(count_lines "$B/keep.rows"), the .txt $(count_lines "$B/txt.rows"); rows whose name, bytes and hashes are the keep's, compared row by row: $nrow_same"
    rows_same() { [ "$(count_lines "$B/keep.rows")" = "$(count_lines "$B/txt.rows")" ] && [ "$nrow_same" = "$(count_lines "$B/keep.rows")" ] && [ "$nrow_same" = "$NPAIRS" ]; }
    check "every .txt row is one kept pair's name, byte counts and sha256s, in name order, one row per pair" "$(yn rows_same)"
    bad_rows=$(tail -n +2 "$TXT" | awk -F'\t' 'NF != 9 || $6 !~ /^(ok|fail|error)$/ || $7 !~ /^(ok|fail|error)$/ || $8 !~ /^(none|refused|count|error)$/ || $9 !~ /^(none|refused|count|error)$/' | wc -l)
    check "every row has nine columns, lo_in and lo each ok, fail or error, and each class none, refused, count or error ($bad_rows rows otherwise)" "$(yn [ "$bad_rows" = 0 ])"
    bad_fit=$(tail -n +2 "$TXT" | awk -F'\t' '{ print $6 ":" $8; print $7 ":" $9 }' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -cvxE 'ok:none|fail:refused|fail:count|error:error')
    check "every side's class fits its verdict ($bad_fit sides otherwise)" "$(yn [ "$bad_fit" = 0 ])"
    stdout_rows() { [ "$(awk -F'\t' 'NF == 3' "$B/oc.stdout")" = "$(tail -n +2 "$TXT" | cut -f1,6,7)" ]; }
    check "the script's per-pair stdout lines are the .txt's test, lo_in and lo columns" "$(yn stdout_rows)"
    echo "command: python3 -I -B <work>/wb.py over each kept input: its xl/workbook.xml entry, its sheet elements by local name (expat, no pattern) and of them those with a prefix"
    cat >"$B/wb.py" <<'PY'
    import sys, zipfile
    from xml.parsers import expat
    for path in sys.argv[1:]:
        name = path.rsplit("/", 1)[1][: -len(".in.xlsx")]
        try:
            z = zipfile.ZipFile(path)
        except zipfile.BadZipFile:
            print("%s\tunreadable\t-\t-" % name)
            continue
        if "xl/workbook.xml" not in z.namelist():
            print("%s\tno\t-\t-" % name)
            continue
        found = {"all": 0, "prefixed": 0}
    
        def start(tag, attrs):
            prefix, _, local = tag.rpartition(":")
            if local == "sheet":
                found["all"] += 1
                found["prefixed"] += 1 if prefix else 0
        p = expat.ParserCreate()
        p.StartElementHandler = start
        try:
            p.Parse(z.read("xl/workbook.xml"), True)
        except expat.ExpatError:
            print("%s\tyes\tunparsed\t-" % name)
            continue
        print("%s\tyes\t%d\t%d" % (name, found["all"], found["prefixed"]))
    PY
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/wb.py"
    python3 -I -B "$B/wb.py" $(sed "s#^#$KEEP/#; s#\$#.in.xlsx#" "$B/pair.names") | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/wb.all"
    echo "  kept inputs by workbook entry and sheet elements (entry, all, prefixed: pairs):"
    cut -f2- "$B/wb.all" | sort | uniq -c | sed 's/^/    /'
    echo "  the .md checked against the .txt and the kept inputs, with the heading specs/0015 P2 verification ruling 1 gives: <work>/mdcheck.py, below"
    cat >"$B/mdcheck.py" <<'PY'
    import sys
    txt, md, wb = sys.argv[1:4]
    rows = [l.split("\t") for l in open(txt).read().split("\n")[1:] if l]
    sheets = {l.split("\t")[0]: l.split("\t")[2] for l in open(wb).read().split("\n") if l}
    text = open(md).read().split("\n")
    REFUSED = ("Inputs refused by LibreOffice (allowed: a fixture LibreOffice cannot load: zip-level,"
               " or a package with no relationships part or an empty content-types root)")
    
    
    def section(title):
        out, on = [], False
        for line in text:
            if line == "## " + title:
                on = True
                continue
            if on and line.startswith("## "):
                break
            if on and line:
                out.append(line)
        return out
    
    
    def listed(names):
        return ["- `%s`" % n for n in names] if names else ["None."]
    
    
    def count(col, v):
        return sum(1 for r in rows if r[col] == v)
    
    
    totals = [len(rows)] + [count(5, v) for v in ("ok", "fail", "error")] + [count(6, v) for v in ("ok", "fail", "error")]
    classes = ["| %s | " % side + " | ".join(str(count(col, c)) for c in ("none", "refused", "count", "error")) + " |"
               for side, col in (("reason_in", 7), ("reason_out", 8))]
    tot = section("Totals")
    checks = [
        ("Totals", tot[2:3] == ["| " + " | ".join(str(t) for t in totals) + " |"] and tot[5:] == classes),
        ("the refused-inputs heading reads as ruled, once", text.count("## " + REFUSED) == 1),
        ("Inputs refused by LibreOffice", section(REFUSED) == listed([r[0] for r in rows if r[7] == "refused"])),
        ("the sheet count did not apply", section("Inputs the sheet count did not apply to (allowed: a workbook fixture with no sheet element)") == listed([r[0] for r in rows if r[7] == "count" and sheets.get(r[0]) == "0"])),
        ("counts differ", section("Inputs whose sheet and table counts differ (a finding)") == listed([r[0] for r in rows if r[7] == "count" and sheets.get(r[0]) != "0"])),
        ("Outputs refused on an accepted input", section("Outputs refused on an input LibreOffice accepted (a finding)") == listed([r[0] for r in rows if r[6] == "fail" and r[5] == "ok"])),
        ("Checks that did not run", section("Checks that did not run (error)") == listed([r[0] for r in rows if "error" in (r[5], r[6])])),
        ("Pairs", section("Pairs")[2:] == ["| `%s` | %s | %s | %s | %s | %s | %s | %s | %s |" % tuple(r) for r in rows]),
        ("the Pairs line", ("- Pairs: %d" % len(rows)) in text),
    ]
    for name, ok in checks:
        print("%s: %s" % (name, "yes" if ok else "no"))
    print("totals: pairs %d; lo_in ok %d fail %d error %d; lo ok %d fail %d error %d" % tuple(totals))
    PY
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/mdcheck.py"
    python3 -I -B "$B/mdcheck.py" "$TXT" "$MD" "$B/wb.all" >"$B/mdcheck.out"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/mdcheck.out"
    md_all() { [ "$(count_matches -E ': yes$' "$B/mdcheck.out")" = 9 ] && [ "$(count_matches -E ': no$' "$B/mdcheck.out")" = 0 ]; }
    check "the .md's nine parts are derived from the .txt and the kept inputs' sheet elements, the heading as ruled" "$(yn md_all)"
    head -n 2 "$TXT" >"$B/c-short.txt"
    python3 -I -B "$B/mdcheck.py" "$B/c-short.txt" "$MD" "$B/wb.all" >"$B/c-mdcheck.out"
    md_ctl() { [ "$(count_matches -E ': no$' "$B/c-mdcheck.out")" -ge 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same check on a .txt cut to one row finds the .md does not match it" "$(yn md_ctl)"
    OLD8=records/m1p8-open-2026-09-24-da080f1
    python3 -I -B "$B/mdcheck.py" "$OLD8.txt" "$OLD8.md" "$B/wb.all" >"$B/c-prevmd.out"
    old_heading() { [ "$(count_matches -F 'the refused-inputs heading reads as ruled, once: no' "$B/c-prevmd.out")" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same check on part 8 P2's committed .md finds the old heading, not the ruled one" "$(yn old_heading)"
    totals_line() { [ "$(sed -n 's/^wrote .*\.txt: \(pairs [^;]*; lo_in [^;]*; lo [^;]*\); inputs refused .*/\1/p' "$B/oc.stdout")" = "$(sed -n 's/^totals: //p' "$B/mdcheck.out")" ]; }
    check "the script's totals line is the totals derived from the .txt" "$(yn totals_line)"
    echo
    echo "### the verdicts against the named record"
    join -t "$TAB" <(tail -n +2 "$B/prev.txt" | cut -f1,6,7,8,9 | LC_ALL=C sort) <(tail -n +2 "$TXT" | cut -f1,6,7,8,9 | LC_ALL=C sort) >"$B/both"
    check "every pair of the named record has a row in this record" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/both")" = "$n_prev" ])"
    awk -F'\t' '$2 != $6 || $3 != $7 || $4 != $8 || $5 != $9 { print $1 "\t" $2 "/" $3 "/" $4 "/" $5 " -> " $6 "/" $7 "/" $8 "/" $9 }' "$B/both" >"$B/moved"
    echo "  the named record's pairs whose lo_in, lo or either class changed: $(count_lines "$B/moved")"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/moved"
    check "no verdict and no class of the named record's pairs moved" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/moved")" = 0 ])"
    printf 'x\tok\tok\tnone\tnone\tok\tfail\tnone\trefused\n' >"$B/c-both"
    moved_ctl() { [ "$(awk -F'\t' '$2 != $6 || $3 != $7 || $4 != $8 || $5 != $9' "$B/c-both" | wc -l)" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same form finds a planted row whose lo moved" "$(yn moved_ctl)"
    echo "  the changed pairs' verdicts (test, lo_in, lo, reason_in, reason_out; none expected, change NWU):"
    join -t "$TAB" "$B/changed.pairs" <(tail -n +2 "$TXT" | cut -f1,6,7,8,9 | LC_ALL=C sort) | sed 's/^/    /'
    echo "  the new pairs' verdicts (test, lo_in, lo, reason_in, reason_out):"
    join -t "$TAB" "$B/new.pairs" <(tail -n +2 "$TXT" | cut -f1,6,7,8,9 | LC_ALL=C sort) | sed 's/^/    /'
    no_new_finding() { [ "$(join -t "$TAB" "$B/new.pairs" <(tail -n +2 "$TXT" | cut -f1,6,7 | LC_ALL=C sort) | awk -F'\t' '$2 == "ok" && $3 != "ok"' | wc -l)" = 0 ]; }
    check "no new pair's output is refused on an accepted input" "$(yn no_new_finding)"
    echo
    echo "### acceptance, and the inputs LibreOffice did not accept"
    tail -n +2 "$TXT" | awk -F'\t' -v OFS='\t' '{ print ($1 ~ /^emend-copy\./ ? "tool" : "crate"), $1, $6, $7, $8, $9 }' >"$B/verdicts"
    for side in crate tool; do
      n=$(awk -F'\t' -v s="$side" '$1 == s' "$B/verdicts" | wc -l)
      nfind=$(awk -F'\t' -v s="$side" '$1 == s && $3 == "ok" && $4 == "fail"' "$B/verdicts" | wc -l)
      nerr=$(awk -F'\t' -v s="$side" '$1 == s && ($3 == "error" || $4 == "error")' "$B/verdicts" | wc -l)
      nin=$(awk -F'\t' -v s="$side" '$1 == s && $3 == "fail"' "$B/verdicts" | wc -l)
      echo "  $side: pairs $n; inputs refused $nin; outputs refused on an accepted input $nfind; checks that did not run $nerr"
      check "$side: no output refused on an accepted input" "$(yn [ "$nfind" = 0 ])"
      check "$side: no check errored" "$(yn [ "$nerr" = 0 ])"
    done
    awk -F'\t' '$5 == "count" { print $2 }' "$B/verdicts" >"$B/count.pairs"
    awk -F'\t' '$2 == "yes" && $3 == "0" { print $1 }' "$B/wb.all" >"$B/zero.pairs"
    echo "  count-class inputs $(count_lines "$B/count.pairs"); kept inputs with a workbook entry and no sheet element $(count_lines "$B/zero.pairs")"
    check "the count-class inputs are exactly the kept inputs with a workbook entry and no sheet element, so no count differs" "$(yn cmp -s "$B/count.pairs" "$B/zero.pairs")"
    echo "  the pairs whose input LibreOffice did not accept, with the class of the input's reason:"
    awk -F'\t' '$3 != "ok" { print $2 "\t" $5 }' "$B/verdicts" | sed 's/^/    /'
    echo
    echo "### the open-check record installed into records/"
    echo "command: install -m 644 <scripts>/out/records/$STEM_OPEN.md <scripts>/out/records/$STEM_OPEN.txt <repo>/$RECORDS_DEST/"
    install -m 644 "$RECORDS/$STEM_OPEN.md" "$RECORDS/$STEM_OPEN.txt" "$RECORDS_DEST"/ && INSTALLED+=("$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM_OPEN.md" "$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM_OPEN.txt")
    echo "  exit: $?"
    for f in "$STEM_OPEN.md" "$STEM_OPEN.txt"; do
      echo "    written <scripts>/out/records/$f: sha256 $(sha_of "$RECORDS/$f"), $(wc -c <"$RECORDS/$f") bytes"
      echo "    installed $RECORDS_DEST/$f: sha256 $(sha_of "$RECORDS_DEST/$f"), $(wc -c <"$RECORDS_DEST/$f") bytes, mode $(stat -c %a "$RECORDS_DEST/$f")"
      check "the installed $f is the written one, byte for byte, mode 644" "$(yn inst_same "$f")"
    done
    fi
    
    echo
    echo "## the record files this run installed hold no path"
    echo "  record files installed by this run: ${#INSTALLED[@]}"
    no_path() {
      local f
      [ "${#INSTALLED[@]}" -ge 1 ] || return 1
      for f in "${INSTALLED[@]}"; do
        [ "$(count_matches -F "$HOME" "$f")" = 0 ] || return 1
        [ "$(count_matches -E '(/home/|/mnt/|/Users/|/tmp/|emend-testing)' "$f")" = 0 ] || return 1
      done
    }
    check "no record file this run installed names <home>, a home, mount, temporary or corpus path" "$(yn no_path)"
    n_inst_want=4
    if [ "$RUN_SKIP_KEEP" = yes ]; then n_inst_want=2; fi
    check "this run installed the record files it writes ($n_inst_want: the sample's pair, and the open pair unless the keep was skipped; changes NUF and NWY)" "$(yn [ "${#INSTALLED[@]}" = "$n_inst_want" ])"
    printf '%s%s%s\n' '/ho' 'me/someone/' 'emend-testing/corpus/x' >"$B/c-path"
    path_ctl() { [ "$(count_matches -E '(/home/|/mnt/|/Users/|/tmp/|emend-testing)' "$B/c-path")" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same form finds a planted path" "$(yn path_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "## status after the run"
    echo "command: git status --porcelain"
    git status --porcelain | sed 's/^/    /'
    st_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    st_ours=$(run_matches -E "$OURS" git status --porcelain)
    echo "  planning's uncommitted spec: $SPEC, sha256 $(sha_of "$SPEC")"
    echo "status lines: $st_all; of them this phase's logs, its record pairs, the API and size records or planning's uncommitted spec and roadmap: $st_ours"
    status_accounted() { [ "$st_all" != error ] && [ "$st_ours" != error ] && [ "$st_all" = "$st_ours" ]; }
    check "every change in the working tree is this phase's, the API and size records, or planning's uncommitted spec and roadmap (change NXG)" "$(yn status_accounted)"
    echo
    echo "## this script's own standard error (specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7)"
    nerr=$(wc -c <"$ERR")
    cp "$ERR" "$B/c-err"; printf 'x' >>"$B/c-err"
    nerr_ctl=$(wc -c <"$B/c-err")
    echo "  command: wc -c <scripts>/out/run.stderr: $nerr bytes; a copy with one byte appended: $nerr_ctl"
    check "this script wrote nothing to its standard error" "$(yn [ "$nerr" = 0 ])"
    check "control: the same count reads one byte more in the copy" "$(yn [ "$nerr_ctl" = "$((nerr + 1))" ])"
    echo "run ended at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    echo "run log checks all as expected: $([ "$fail" -eq 0 ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    exec 1>&3
    wait "$SCRUB_PID" 2>/dev/null
    exit "$fail"

## the shared counting library this log sources (the phase commit's, by git show; change NSB)
    # emend shared counting forms (specs/0007-gate-self-test.md, "scripts/counting.sh").
    #
    # Sourced by scripts/gate-self-test.sh and by the log scripts of later phases,
    # which use these instead of carrying their own copy.
    #
    # WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. In T3 P4 four counting sites compared a bare `grep -c`
    # with 0 without reading the exit status, so a read error printed 0 and the
    # check passed. Two independent checks found them, and the class was declared
    # closed three further times while instances still stood: a helper whose first
    # repair read grep's status while `cat` was the failing command, and both
    # halves of one function in T2 P7. Planning's remedy is that every counting
    # form, including a throwaway one, is a named function that reads the exit
    # status and has a positive control, from the start.
    #
    # Every function prints either a number or the word "error". None of them ever
    # prints a matched line, a value, or a path. A caller that compares a result
    # with 0 therefore cannot mistake a failed read for an absence.
    #
    # counting_controls runs every form against a match, a miss and an unreadable
    # file, prints one line per control, and sets counting_controls_ok. Callers run
    # it before using any form.
    
    G=/usr/bin/grep
    
    # count_matches <-F|-E> <pattern> <file>...: total matching lines across the
    # files, or "error" if any file could not be read. The files go to grep
    # directly: with `cat file | grep -c`, an unreadable file makes CAT fail while
    # grep counts 0 over the empty stream and exits 1, so the read error reads as
    # "no hits".
    count_matches() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c "$mode" -e "$pattern" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # count_from_file <-F|-E> <pattern file> <file>...: the same, with the patterns
    # read from a file (grep -f), so a pattern is never printed.
    count_from_file() {
      local mode=$1 patterns=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c "$mode" -f "$patterns" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # count_bytes <tr class> <file>...: total bytes of that class across the files,
    # or "error" if any file could not be read. Each file is read on its own rather
    # than through `cat "$@" | tr`, for the same reason as above.
    count_bytes() {
      local class=$1 total=0 f n
      shift
      for f in "$@"; do
        [ -r "$f" ] || { printf 'error'; return; }
        n=$(LC_ALL=C tr -cd "$class" <"$f" | wc -c) || { printf 'error'; return; }
        total=$((total + n))
      done
      printf '%s' "$total"
    }
    
    # count_lines <file>...: total lines, or "error" if any file could not be read.
    count_lines() {
      local total=0 f n
      for f in "$@"; do
        [ -r "$f" ] || { printf 'error'; return; }
        n=$(wc -l <"$f") || { printf 'error'; return; }
        total=$((total + n))
      done
      printf '%s' "$total"
    }
    
    # count_matches_i <-F|-E> <pattern> <file>...: count_matches with -i, the form
    # the hygiene step uses for OFFICE_RE and ZONE_RE. It lived in a log script as a
    # hand-rolled copy with no control of its own (independent check 2, T6 P1, gap
    # 14); a counting form belongs here, with a control, even a throwaway one.
    count_matches_i() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c -i "$mode" -e "$pattern" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # run_lines <command...>: run the command, and print the number of lines it
    # wrote on stdout, or "error" if the command itself failed. The log scripts
    # asserted a clean working tree with
    #   git status --porcelain >file 2>/dev/null || : >file
    # which turns a FAILED git status into an empty file, so the check read a
    # failed command as a clean tree (independent check 2, T6 P1, gap 1; planning
    # reproduced it). Reading the command's exit status is the whole point: a
    # command that could not run is never the same as a command that found nothing.
    run_lines() {
      local out rc
      out=$("$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ -z "$out" ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | wc -l | tr -d ' '
    }
    
    # run_matches <-F|-E> <pattern> <command...>: the same, counting only the lines
    # that match, so a caller can compare "all lines" with "lines of the expected
    # shape" without either count hiding a failed command.
    run_matches() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$("$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ -z "$out" ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -c "$mode" -e "$pattern" || true
    }
    
    CTRL_CLASS='\000-\010\013\014\016-\037\177'
    NONASCII_CLASS='\200-\377'
    
    # counting_controls <label prefix>: run every counting form above against a
    # fixture that must match and one that must not, and against an unreadable
    # file, printing one line per result. Sets counting_controls_ok to yes or no.
    # This is the positive control planning requires for every form, and it also
    # proves each form reports "error" rather than 0 when it cannot read.
    counting_controls() {
      local d ok=yes r
      d=$(mktemp -d) || { counting_controls_ok=no; return; }
      printf 'alpha\nbeta needle gamma\nneedle\n' >"$d/hit"
      printf 'nothing of interest\n' >"$d/miss"
      printf 'x \033[31mred\033[m\017 y\ncaf\303\251\n' >"$d/bytes"
      printf 'needle\n' >"$d/patterns"
      printf 'unreadable\n' >"$d/locked"
      chmod 000 "$d/locked"
    
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit");        echo "  control count_matches on a file with two matching lines: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/miss");       echo "  control count_matches on a file with none: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit" "$d/miss"); echo "  control count_matches summed over two files: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -E 'ne+dle' "$d/hit");      echo "  control count_matches with a regular expression: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/locked");     echo "  control count_matches on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit" "$d/locked"); echo "  control count_matches on readable plus unreadable: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/hit"); echo "  control count_from_file on the same file: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/miss"); echo "  control count_from_file on a file with none: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/locked"); echo "  control count_from_file on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/bytes");    echo "  control count_bytes, control bytes in a file with ESC, ESC and SI: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$NONASCII_CLASS" "$d/bytes"); echo "  control count_bytes, non-ASCII bytes in a file with one two-byte character: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/miss");     echo "  control count_bytes on a clean file: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/locked");   echo "  control count_bytes on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_lines "$d/hit");                    echo "  control count_lines on a three-line file: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_lines "$d/locked");                 echo "  control count_lines on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      printf 'NEEDLE\nneedle\n' >"$d/mixedcase"
      r=$(count_matches_i -F needle "$d/mixedcase"); echo "  control count_matches_i on mixed case: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/mixedcase");  echo "  control count_matches on the same file, case sensitive: $r (expect 1)"; [ "$r" = 1 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches_i -F needle "$d/locked");   echo "  control count_matches_i on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines printf 'a\nb\nc\n');            echo "  control run_lines on a command printing three lines: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines true);                          echo "  control run_lines on a command printing nothing: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines false);                         echo "  control run_lines on a FAILING command: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines "$d/no-such-command");          echo "  control run_lines on a command that cannot run: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_matches -F needle printf 'needle\nother\n'); echo "  control run_matches on a command printing one match: $r (expect 1)"; [ "$r" = 1 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_matches -F needle false);             echo "  control run_matches on a FAILING command: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
    
      chmod 644 "$d/locked"
      rm -rf "${d:?}"
      counting_controls_ok=$ok
      echo "  counting controls: $([ "$ok" = yes ] && echo "all as expected" || echo FAILED)"
    }

## counting controls
  control count_matches on a file with two matching lines: 2 (expect 2)
  control count_matches on a file with none: 0 (expect 0)
  control count_matches summed over two files: 2 (expect 2)
  control count_matches with a regular expression: 2 (expect 2)
  control count_matches on an unreadable file: error (expect error)
  control count_matches on readable plus unreadable: error (expect error)
  control count_from_file on the same file: 2 (expect 2)
